var tafsirData_4 = {
  "1": "O humanity, be mindful of your Lord who created you from a single soul — from it He created its mate — and from both spread many men and women. And be mindful of Allah, by whom you ask one another, and of family ties — Allah is ever Watchful over you.\n\nYa ayyuha an-nas — O humanity — same universal call as earlier in al-Baqarah (2:21) worship your Lord. Here fear your Lord who created you from single soul — nafs wahidah — Adam — and from it created its mate — Hawwa from rib? From same essence, so equal origin.\n\nWa baththa minhuma rijalan kathiran wa nisa — and spread from both many men and women — population from one pair, bonding humanity as one family.\n\nWattaqu Allaha alladhi tasa'aluna bihi wal-arham — Be mindful Allah by whom you ask one another and family ties — In pre-Islam they would say As'aluka billah — I ask you by Allah — and ask by womb ties. Preserve both.\n\nInna Allaha kana alaykum Raqiba — Allah ever Watchful over you — Raqib — Observant, Guardian. Same as nothing hidden (3:5), knows what in chests.\n\nThis verse foundation of An-Nisa — Women — because it begins humanity from one soul and mate, establishing equality origin, spread, and sanctity wombs. Marriage, inheritance, orphan care all branch from family tie sanctity.\n\nIf single soul origin, then racism, tribalism collapse. And if Allah Watchful, orphan wealth (next verse) cannot be swallowed unseen.\n\nIt also answers those who think woman inferior creation. From same soul, created mate from it — together building.\n\nSo God-consciousness includes consciousness of womb ties.\n\nNext orphan wealth.",
  "2": "Give orphans their wealth when they reach maturity, and do not exchange worthless of yours for their good, nor consume their wealth with your wealth — it is a great sin.\n\nWa atu al-yatama amwalahum — Give orphans their wealth — when rushd — maturity of mind, not just age.\n\nWa la tatabaddalu al-khabitha bit-tayyib — Do not exchange bad for good — al-khabith — worthless, bad — with tayyib — good, valuable. Guardians would take orphan's healthy sheep giving sick one, or fine date palm giving dead one, thinking orphan won't notice.\n\nWa la ta'kulu amwalahum ila amwalikum — Do not eat their wealth along with your wealth — mixing to confuse.\n\nInnahu kana huban kabira — It is great sin — hub — sin.\n\nOrphan care mentioned after womb ties because orphan most vulnerable family tie severed by death.\n\nMaturing concept: physical puberty not enough; rushd — ability manage wealth responsibly. Until then protect, invest, test.\n\nDo not exchange — khabith tayyib contrast earlier (2:267) do not aim for bad to spend while you would not take except closing eyes — same principle: do not give orphan bad taking good.\n\nGreat sin because orphan weak, no father to defend, but Allah Raqib Watchful earlier sees.\n\nModern application: managing orphan funds, charity funds, inheritance for minors — mixing personal business with orphan's account — prohibited.\n\nNext if fear fail give orphan women due rights then marry other women.",
  "3": "If you fear you will not do justice to orphan women — then marry other women you like — two, three, four — but if fear you cannot be just, then one — or what your right hand possesses — that is more likely you will not be unfair.\n\nFe-orhan women — yatama — girls under guardianship whose wealth you manage — temptation to marry them without proper mahr to keep wealth, or to oppress. If fear injustice to them, then marry other women you like — ghayr — not from among them.\n\nMathna wa thulatha wa ruba — two three four — permission polygyny with limit four — pre-Islam unlimited. Permission not command.\n\nFa-in khiftum alla ta'dilu fa-wahidah — If fear not just — justice — then one. Justice here includes time, support, kindness, division nights housing? Not love feeling but equity.\n\nAw ma malakat aymanukum — or right hand possesses — slave women context where no polygyny justice required same? Historical.\n\nDhalika adna alla ta'ulu — This more likely you not be unfair — ta'ulu — deviate, be burdened with many dependents unjustly.\n\nThis verse often misread divorced from orphan context. It came to protect orphans, not to promote desire. Polygyny conditional justice, justice itself condition fears — then one.\n\nJustice among wives great responsibility — Prophet said whoever has two wives and inclines to one will come Day Resurrection with one side drooping.\n\nIf unable justice then one — Quran sets monogamy as closest to fairness.\n\nSo verse: protect orphan women wealth rights — if fear injustice marrying them, marry others up to four; fear injustice among them — one.\n\nNext give women dowries graciously.",
  "4": "Give women their dowries graciously — but if they willingly waive some, enjoy it freely with wholesome pleasure.\n\nWa atu an-nisa saduqatihinna nihlah — Give women saduqat — dowries — nihlah — graciously, gift, cheerfully — not as price purchase but as gift honour.\n\nOrphan girls just mentioned often married without proper mahr; this general command gives women dowry as right, not father's property.\n\nFa-in tibna lakum an shay'in minhu nafsan fa-kuluhu hani'an mari'an — But if they willingly waive some of it — about part of mahr — with good will of self — then eat it — i.e., use it — hani'an mari'an — freely wholesome pleasant — pleasure without sin.\n\nNafs — willingness — important: coercion invalidates. Waiving must be happy heart, not pressured by family or guilt.\n\nThis transforms dowry from transaction to gift and then potentially shared gift if she chooses.\n\nShows woman's financial independence: mahr hers, can give back willingly if wants, husband may enjoy but only with her willing waiver.\n\nConnects to earlier give orphans wealth (2) — both about returning property to rightful owners: orphans, women.\n\nModern: cultural practices where father or family takes mahr — prohibited; it's hers.\n\nNext do not entrust incapable among dependants with wealth that Allah made support.",
  "5": "Do not give those weak-minded your wealth which Allah made as support for you — but feed and clothe them from it and speak to them kind words.\n\nWa la tu'tu as-sufaha amwalakum — Do not entrust incapable — sufaha — weak-minded, immature, prodigal, cannot manage wealth responsibly — your wealth which Allah made qiyam — support standing for you — qiyaman — means of support.\n\nBut feed clothe them from it — feed clothe — maintain — and speak kind words — qawlan ma'rufan — gentle.\n\nWho are sufaha? Orphans not reached rushd, minors, those with mental incapacity, or spendthrift who would waste.\n\nWealth Allah made means support — qiyam — survival, not to be thrown away. Owner — your wealth? Actually orphan's wealth but called your wealth because community trust? Or guardian's own wealth should not be given to incapable who will waste, causing family collapse.\n\nBalance: protect wealth but maintain compassion — feed clothe speak kind, not harshly refuse.\n\nThis verse precedes testing orphans (6) — do not give wealth yet, but care.\n\nIt also shows wealth responsibility: wealth is standing of community — if wasted society collapses.\n\nKind words — as earlier (2:263) kind words better than charity followed by injury — even refusing to hand large sum should be with kind words.\n\nNext test orphans.",
  "6": "Test orphans until they reach marriageable age — if you perceive sound judgment in them, give them their wealth — do not consume it wastefully hastily before they grow — whoever rich should abstain, whoever poor may eat fairly — when you hand wealth, take witnesses — Allah suffices as Reckoner.\n\nWabtulu al-yatama hatta idha balaghu an-nikah — Test orphans until reach marriage age — test with small business, responsibility.\n\nFa-in anastum minhum rushdan — If perceive rushd — sound judgment — fa-dfa'u ilayhim amwalahum — give their wealth.\n\nWa la ta'kuluha israfan wa bidaran an yakbaru — Do not eat it wastefully hastily before they grow — israf — waste, bidar — hastening fear they will grow and take it, so spending quickly to prevent.\n\nWa man kana ghaniyyan fal-yastafif wa man kana faqiran fal-ya'kul bil-ma'ruf — Whoever rich among guardians should abstain — not take wage for managing; poor may eat fairly — reasonable fee for work.\n\nFa-idha dafa'tum ilayhim amwalahum fa-ashhidu alayhim — When handing wealth take witnesses — protect both.\n\nWa kafa billahi Hasiba — Allah suffices as Reckoner — Hasib — computes, knows how managed, will ask.\n\nSequence orphans: give when maturity (2), do not exchange bad good (2), fear justice orphan women (3), now test until rushd, do not hastily eat, rich abstain poor eat fairly, witnesses, Allah Hasib.\n\nComplete system protecting vulnerable from guardian greed and from own immaturity.\n\nFor modern fund managers, trustees, will executors — perfect guidance.\n\nNext shares of inheritance.",
  "7": "Men have share of what parents and close relatives leave — women have share of what parents and close relatives leave — whether little or much — ordained share.\n\nLir-rijali nasibun mimma taraka al-walidan wal-aqrabun wa lin-nisa nasibun... — Men have share what parents close relatives leave, women have share — both.\n\nPre-Islam women had no inheritance; some cultures said women lack intellect battle. Quran declares nasib — share — for women as for men, little or much.\n\nNasiban mafrudan — ordained obligatory share — mafrud — fixed, decreed. Not charity optional.\n\nThis verse foundation inheritance law detailed next.\n\nIt follows orphan wealth protection because inheritance often source orphan wealth. Ensuring women share prevents ancient injustice where male relatives took all.\n\nLineage closeness matters: parents, aqrabun.\n\nWhether little much — qalilan aw kathiran — no minimum threshold; even small estate divided as per share.\n\nMafrudan — implies fixed by Allah not by whim, so no one can deprive.\n\nFor today where cultural practice deprives daughters — contradicts ordained share. Quran says share for women.\n\nNext if relatives, orphans, poor present at division.",
  "8": "If at division relatives, orphans, poor are present, provide for them from it and speak to them kind words.\n\nWa idha hadara al-qismata ulu al-qurba wal-yatama wal-masakin farzuquhum minhu wa qulu lahum qawlan ma'rufan — If at division relatives non-heirs, orphans, poor present at inheritance distribution — give them something — farzuquhum minhu — provide from it.\n\nWa qulu qawlan ma'rufan — Speak kind words.\n\nDivision can be painful for those present who hoped share but not heir — distant relatives, orphan neighbours, poor who came.\n\nIslam teaches not to ignore them heart broken watching. Give something from estate before fixed shares? Scholars: from third after bequests? Or from own generosity? Either, provide.\n\nAnd kind words — explain, comfort, not harshly turn away — as earlier kind words better than charity followed by injury (2:263) and kind words before entrusting incapable (5).\n\nThis verse softens fixed inheritance with voluntary benevolence.\n\nEncourages compassion: formal shares must be exact, but kindness beyond formal shares also needed.\n\nNext let those fear leaving weak offspring behind.",
  "9": "Let those fear who, if they left behind weak offspring, would be concerned for them — so let them be mindful of Allah and speak right words.\n\nWalyakhsha alladhina law taraku min khalfihim dhurriyyatan di'afan khafu alayhim — Let fear those who if leaving weak offspring would worry — dhurriyyah di'af — weak children — khafu — concerned.\n\nFalyattaqu Allaha wal-yaqulu qawlan sadida — Be mindful Allah and speak right words — sadida — straight, correct, right.\n\nContext: guardians managing orphan wealth or persons making bequests: imagine your own weak children left behind orphaned, how would you want them treated? Fear that scenario. Then treat orphans in your care as you would want your weak children treated.\n\nQawlan sadida — right words — honest, straight — as earlier kind words but here sadida — correct, not manipulative.\n\nIf you would not want your children deprived, do not deprive others.\n\nEmpathy principle: put yourself place orphan's father.\n\nThis verse moves from law to conscience — Raqib Watchful knows if you treat weak children as you treat your own.\n\nNext those who consume orphans wealth unjustly.",
  "10": "Those who consume orphans' wealth unjustly — they only consume fire into bellies — they will burn in Blaze.\n\nInna alladhina ya'kuluna amwala al-yatama zulman innama ya'kuluna fi butunihim naran wa sa-yaslawna sa'ira — Those eat orphans wealth unjustly — zulman — wrongfully — innama ya'kuluna fi butunihim nar — only consume fire into bellies — what they think eat wealth is actually fire.\n\nWa sa-yaslawna sa'ira — Will burn Blaze — sa'ir — flaming fire.\n\nEarlier (2:174) those conceal Book and exchange small price consume nothing but Fire into bellies — same consumption imagery linking wealth unjust consumption to eating Fire. Orphan wealth and hiding knowledge both considered fire in belly.\n\nPreceding verses gave protection system: give when maturity, not exchange bad good, not hastily eat, rich abstain poor eat fairly, witnesses, Allah Hasib. Now consequence eating unjustly.\n\nThis warns guardian: transaction may look profitable in ledger but belly filled fire and final destination Blaze.\n\nFor modern charity worker who takes from orphan sponsorship fund — same threat.\n\nAfter this severe warning, detailed inheritance shares come — to prevent disputes leading to such consumption.\n\nNext Allah instructs you concerning children.",
  "11": "Allah instructs you concerning your children — for male like share of two females — if there are only daughters, two or more, two-thirds; if one, half; for parents each sixth if child left; if no child and parents only heirs, mother third; if siblings, mother sixth after bequest or debt — parents and children you don't know who more beneficial — ordained from Allah — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nYusikum Allahu fi awladikum li-dhakari mithlu hazzi al-unthayayin... — Central inheritance verse. For male like share two females — not because worth difference but responsibility: male qawwam — maintainer provides mahr, maintenance wife children, defence, blood money, etc. Female share often kept as pure savings.\n\nIf daughters only — two or more two-thirds; one daughter half.\n\nParents: if deceased left child, each parent sixth; if no child parents only heirs, mother third father remainder; if siblings exist mother sixth (due crowd).\n\nMin ba'di wasiyyatin yusi biha aw dayn — After bequest he ordains or debt — bequest debt settled before division — shows rights of dead honoured before heirs.\n\nAba'ukum wa abna'ukum la tadruna ayyuhum aqrabu lakum naf'an — Fathers children you don't know who nearer benefit — you might think son more beneficial but daughter more caring, etc. — leave division to Knower.\n\nFaridatan min Allah — ordained from Allah — as earlier share ordained (7).\n\nInnAllaha kana Aliman Hakima — Knowing, Wise — same closing as earlier shaping wombs as wills (3:6) and providing without account — He knows benefit, places shares with wisdom.\n\nThis verse transforms Jahiliyyah deprivation into precise math mercy.\n\nFor today, calculate with care, use trustworthy scholar, not emotions.\n\nNext shares spouses and calibration.",
  "12": "And for you half of what wives leave if no child — if child then quarter — for them quarter of what you leave if no child — if child then eighth — after bequest or debt — if man or woman leaves no parent nor child but has brother sister each sixth; if more than that they share third — after bequest or debt not harming — bequest from Allah — Allah Knowing, Forbearing.\n\nSpouses shares: husband gets half wife's estate if no child, quarter if child; wife gets quarter husband's if no child, eighth if child — if multiple wives share quarter/eighth equally.\n\nAfter bequest or debt — again.\n\nKalalah — one leaves no parent child but sibling — each sibling sixth, more than one share third equally male female — unique case siblings share equally.\n\nGhayra mudar — not harming — bequest should not intend harm heirs by exceeding third or favouritism.\n\nWasiyyatan min Allah — Bequest from Allah — as wasiyyah Allah gave you? Or instruction from Allah — Allah Knowing Forbearing — Halim — tolerant, not hastening punishment for mistakes inheritance but knows.\n\nThis verse completes obligatory shares: children, parents, spouses, siblings kalalah.\n\nShares intricate but purpose: preserve womb ties, protect weak, prevent hoarding, distribute.\n\nEarlier (2:180) bequest parents close relatives — now detailed shares abrogate? Scholars say detailed shares replace earlier general bequest but bequest for non-heirs up to third remains.\n\nFear leaving weak offspring (9) addressed: fixed shares prevent leaving weak destitute?\n\nNext those limits Allah.",
  "13": "These are limits of Allah — whoever obeys Allah and Messenger will be admitted to Gardens beneath rivers flow abiding forever — that is great success.\n\nTilka hududu Allah — These limits Allah — hudud — boundaries — inheritance shares are hudud not suggestion.\n\nWa man yuti'illaha wa rasulahu yudkhilhu jannatin... — Obeys Allah and Messenger admitted Gardens rivers forever — great success — fawz azim.\n\nObedience in dividing precisely as commanded, not manipulating with tricks, leads Gardens.\n\nAfter detailed math, promise Gardens — shows importance.\n\nLimits protect: if crossed, great sin.\n\nNext whoever disobeys limits transgresses will enter Fire.",
  "14": "Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger and transgresses His limits — He will put him in Fire abiding therein — humiliating punishment.\n\nWa man ya'si Allaha wa rasulahu wa yata'adda hududahu yudkhilhu naran khalidan fiha wa lahu adhabun muhin — Disobeys Allah Messenger transgresses limits — enter Fire abiding — punishment humiliating — muhin — humiliating, as earlier disgrace struck (3:112).\n\nIf obedience Gardens great success, disobedience Fire humiliating.\n\nHudud Allah repeated many times around marriage divorce inheritance — boundaries protect family and society.\n\nTransgression includes depriving female heirs, taking orphan wealth, making harmful bequest.\n\nHumble adherence brings Gardens, arrogance crossing limits brings Fire humiliation.\n\nAfter inheritance, next verse about immorality women.",
  "15": "Those who commit immorality among your women — bring four witnesses among you — if they testify confine them in houses until death takes them or Allah makes way for them.\n\nWallati ya'tina al-fahishata min nisa'ikum fastashhidu alayhinna arba'atan minkum — Women commit fahishah — adultery — bring four witnesses from you — four to prove, strict proof to avoid slander.\n\nFa-in shahidu fa-amsikuhunna fil-buyut hatta yatawaffahunna al-mawt aw yaj'ala Allahu lahunna sabila — If testify confine houses until death or Allah makes way — sabila — way out.\n\nEarly ruling confinement until later abrogated by flogging 100 lashes for unmarried and stoning married? Scholars differ; Quranic later verse (24:2) provides lashes, Sunnah adds.\n\n\"Allah makes way\" — indicates early temporary ruling awaiting further legislation.\n\nFour witnesses requirement protects chastity from accusation.\n\nThis verse after inheritance shows family protection not only wealth but chastity.\n\nNext two men immorality.",
  "16": "And the two among you who commit it — punish them — if they repent and correct, leave them alone — Allah is Ever Accepting repentance, Merciful.\n\nWalladhani ya'tiyaniha minkum fa-adhuhuma — Two among you commit — lesbians? Actually two men? Scholars said two men adultery? Or man woman? Adhuhuma — punish them — harm — ta'zir.\n\nFa-in taba wa aslahā fa-a'ridu anhuma — If repent and correct leave them.\n\nInna Allaha kana Tawwaba Rahima — Ever Accepting repentance Merciful.\n\nEarly ruling mild punishment then if repent leave.\n\nLater detailed hadd punishments came.\n\nPurpose: purify society while opening repentance door.\n\nVerses 15-16 show gradual legislation: confinement, harm, then later fixed hadd.\n\nOpening repentance door consistent pattern: except those repent correct (2:160, 3:89).\n\nNext repentance time.",
  "17": "Repentance with Allah is only for those who do evil in ignorance then repent soon — they Allah will turn to — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nInnama at-tawbatu alalLahi lilladhina ya'maluna as-su'a bi-jahalah thumma yatubuna min qaribin — Repentance with Allah is for those do evil in ignorance then repent soon — qarib — soon after, before death.\n\nFa-ula'ika yatubu Allahu alayhim wa kan Allahu Aliman Hakima — Will turn — Allah Knowing Wise.\n\nJahalah — ignorance — not lack knowledge that it's wrong, but ignorance of consequences? Or committing in state of overwhelming desire ignorance that soul forgets Allah — all sin done in jahalah sense.\n\nMin qarib — soon — before death, before final rattle.\n\nAllah Knowing Wise knows who sincere soon vs delay.\n\nNext not for those continue evil deeds until death comes.",
  "18": "Not for those who continue doing evil until death approaches one of them and says now I repent — nor those who die disbelievers — painful punishment.\n\nWa laysat at-tawbatu lilladhina ya'maluna as-sayyi'at hatta idha hadara ahadahum al-mawtu qala inni tubtu al-ana wa la alladhina yamutuna wa hum kuffar — Not for those continue evil until death approaches one says now repent — nor those die disbelievers.\n\nUla'ika a'tadna lahum adhaban alima — Painful punishment.\n\nRepentance at deathbed after life of persistence not accepted, as Pharaoh when drowning said believed.\n\nSoon repentance accepted, death rattle repentance not.\n\nThose die disbelievers not accepted even earth full gold earlier.\n\nThus time window for repentance limited.\n\nNext prohibition inheriting women by force.",
  "19": "O you who believe, it is not lawful for you to inherit women by force — nor prevent them to take back part of what you gave them unless they commit clear immorality — live with them in kindness — if you dislike them perhaps you dislike something Allah placed much good in.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la yahillu lakum an tarithu an-nisa karhan — Not lawful inherit women by force — pre-Islam when man died, his heir would inherit widow as property, marry without mahr or prevent marriage to take ransom.\n\nWa la ta'duluhunna li-tadhhabu bi-ba'di ma ataytumuhunna illa an ya'tina bi-fahishatin mubayyinah — Not prevent them to take back part dowry unless clear immorality.\n\nWa ashiruhunna bil-ma'ruf — Live with them in kindness — ma'ruf.\n\nFa-in karihtumuhunna fa-asa an takrahu shay'an wa yaj'ala Allahu fihi khayran kathira — If dislike them perhaps dislike something Allah placed much good — khayr kathir — much good — child, compassion later, etc.\n\nThis verse after repentance shows marriage respect: women not property inherited.\n\nLive with kindness — includes spending beloved, restraining anger pardoning (3:134).\n\nIf dislike, patience may reveal much good — dislike may be temporary due to behaviour; patience reveals goodness.\n\nProphet said believing man should not hate believing woman if dislike one trait pleased with another.\n\nNext tighten marriage prohibitions.\n\nAfter inheritance and orphans, marriage kindness foundation.",
  "20": "If you wish to replace wife with another and you gave one of them qintar — heap — do not take anything from it — will you take it by slander and clear sin? And how will you take it after you were intimate and they took from you firm covenant?\n\nWa in aradtum istibdala zawjin makana zawjin wa ataytum ihdahunna qintaran fa-la ta'khudhu minhu shay'an — If replace wife with another and gave one qintar heap — large mahr — do not take anything.\n\nA-ta'khudhunahu buhtanan wa ithman mubina — Take by slander clear sin? Accusing her immorality to justify taking mahr.\n\nWa kayfa ta'khudhuna wa qad afda ba'dukum ila ba'd wa akhadhna minkum mithaqan ghaliza — How take after intimate — afda — some to other — and they took from you firm covenant — mithaq ghaliz — solemn covenant.\n\nMithaq ghaliz used only for marriage and for prophets covenant — shows marriage serious.\n\nQintar — even huge mahr — once given cannot be reclaimed upon divorce to replace.\n\nEarlier (2:229) not lawful take back anything gave except khul' case. Here emphasises no reclaim even heap.\n\nBuhtan — slander — and ithm mubin — clear sin — double crime.\n\nFirm covenant — marriage covenant — includes kindness living, protecting.\n\nFor today's divorces where husband demands return mahr or gifts — prohibited unless she initiates khul' and returns willingly.\n\nNext prohibited women to marry.",
  "21": "And do not marry women your fathers married, except what passed — it is immorality, hated, and evil way. Wa la tankihu ma nakaha aba'ukum min an-nisa illa ma qad salaf — Do not marry women fathers married — stepmothers — except past before prohibition — innahu kana fahishatan wa maqtan wa sa'a sabila — immorality, hated, evil way — fahishah, maqt — hated by Allah and people, sa'a sabil — evil path.\n\nPre-Islam would inherit stepmother as part of estate. This abolishes.\n\nMarriage sanctity family ties: father wife like mother prohibition.\n\nPassed exception — before Islam not punished.\n\nLink to earlier do not inherit women by force (19) — similar.\n\nNext detailed mahram list.",
  "22": "Forbidden to you are mothers, daughters, sisters, paternal aunts, maternal aunts, brother's daughters, sister's daughters, milk-mothers who nursed you, milk-sisters, mothers of wives, stepdaughters under guardianship from wives you consummated — if not consummated no blame — wives of your sons from your loins, and to combine two sisters — except past — Allah Forgiving, Merciful.\n\nHurremat alaykum... — Detailed mahram list permanently forbidden:\n\nLineal ascend: mothers, grandmothers, daughters granddaughters, sisters, aunts paternal maternal, brother's daughters sister's daughters — blood.\n\nMilk: mothers who nursed you, milk sisters — rada' — similar to blood because milk creates bone flesh.\n\nMarriage: mothers of wives — once marry wife her mother forbidden even before consummation; stepdaughters under guardianship — rabibah — from wives you consummated — if not consummated, not forbidden; wives of sons from loins — daughter-in-law forbidden; combine two sisters at same time — cannot marry sister of wife while wife alive and marriage existing — except past.\n\nAllah Forgiving Merciful — Ghafur Rahim — past before prohibition forgiven.\n\nThis list protects family structure, genetics, avoids confusion.\n\nNext lawful beyond that.\n\nNote mahram list includes milk which modern genetics still relevant? milk kinship creates bonding.\n\nFor believer, memorizing list essential for marriage validity.",
  "23": "And lawful beyond that that you seek with your wealth desiring chastity not lust — for what you enjoy from them give their dowries as obligation — there is no blame if you both agree after obligation — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nWa uhilla lakum ma wara'a dhalikum an tabtaghu bi-amwalikum muhsinin ghayra musafihin — Beyond prohibited list lawful to seek with wealth desiring chastity not lust — muhsinin — guarding chastity, ghayra musafihin — not fornicators.\n\nFama istamta'tum bihi minhunna fa-atuhunna ujurahunna faridah — For what you enjoy from them give dowries as obligation — faridah — fixed.\n\nWa la junaha alaykum fi-ma taradaytum bihi min ba'di al-faridah — No blame if both agree after obligation — additional gift or waiver after.\n\nInnAllaha kana Aliman Hakima — Knowing Wise.\n\nIhsanin vs safih — marriage for chastity vs lust.\n\nSeeking with wealth indicates man spends mahr, maintenance — financial responsibility.\n\nEnjoyment — istimta — includes intimacy, companionship.\n\nDowry faridah — obligatory as earlier nihlah graciously (4).\n\nMutual agreement after obligation allows adjusting mahr.\n\nKnowing Wise — knows intention chastity vs lust.\n\nNext unable to marry free believing women then from believing slave girls.",
  "24": "Whoever cannot afford to marry free believing women — then from believing slave girls your right hands possess — Allah knows your faith — you are from one another — marry them with permission of owners and give dowries in kindness as chaste not fornicators nor secret lovers — when married if commit immorality their punishment half of free — that for those fear difficulty — patience better — Allah Forgiving, Merciful.\n\nWa man lam yastati' minkum tawlan an yankiha al-muhsanati al-mu'minati fa-mimma malakat aymanukum min fatayatikum al-mu'minati — Whoever cannot afford tawl — means — to marry free chaste believing women — then from believing slave girls right hands possess.\n\nWallahu A'lamu bi-imanikum ba'dukum min ba'd — Allah knows faith — you from one another — no superiority free vs slave in faith, all from one soul (1).\n\nFanki'huhunna bi-idhni ahlihinna wa atuhunna ujura hunna bil-ma'ruf muhsanatin ghayra musafihatin wa la muttakhidhati akhdan — Marry with permission owners, give dowries kindness as chaste not fornicators nor secret lovers.\n\nFa-idha uhsinna fa-in atayna bi-fahishatin fa-alayhinna nisfu ma ala al-muhsanati min al-adhab — When married if commit immorality punishment half free — because slave status lighter? Deterrence but mercy.\n\nDhalika liman khashiya al-anat minkum wa an tasbiru khayrun lakum — That for those fear difficulty — anat — hardship sin fornication — patience better.\n\nWallahu Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving Merciful — for those who fall.\n\nThis verse shows Islam gradual emancipation encouraging marriage slaves giving rights, not exploiting.\n\nPatience better than marrying slave if can avoid? Shows chastity priority but patience higher.\n\nNext Allah wants to make clear guide you to ways before.",
  "25": "Allah wants to make clear to you and guide you to ways of those before you and turn to you — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nYuridu Allahu li-yubayyina lakum wa yahdiyakum sunana alladhina min qablikum wa yatuba alaykum — Allah wants to make clear, guide to ways those before — sunan — patterns of previous righteous nations who handled marriage inheritance purification.\n\nWa yatuba alaykum — Turn to you — tawbah — accept repentance.\n\nWallahu Alimun Hakim — Knowing Wise — knows needs, guides wisely.\n\nAfter detailed mahram and marriage rules, reminder purpose: clarity, guidance to righteous ways, tawbah acceptance.\n\nSunana alladhina min qablikum — ways before includes Ibrahim hanif, family Imran, etc.\n\nBayan — clarification — as earlier Allah makes clear signs so you may understand (2:242, 3:103). Clarity mercy.\n\nKnowing Wise — same closing as earlier inheritance (11,12).\n\nNext Allah wants to turn to you but those follow desires want you to deviate great deviation.",
  "26": "Allah wants to turn to you, but those who follow desires want you to deviate great deviation. Wallahu yuridu an yatuba alaykum wa yuridu alladhina yattabi'una ash-shahawati an tamilu maylan azima — Allah wants to turn to you — tawbah — but followers desires — shahawat — zina, riba, mixing truth falsehood — want you deviate great deviation.\n\nTamilu maylan azima — great deviation — like making lawful unlawful, normalizing fornication as consensual, etc.\n\nContrast: Allah wants bayan, guidance, tawbah; desire followers want deviation great.\n\nEarlier Satan threatens poverty orders immorality (2:268), steps of Satan (2:168). Here followers desires explicit.\n\nSo two calls: call to Jannah forgiveness with permission (2:221) vs call to Fire.\n\nFor believer choosing marriage chaste (23) vs lust, choosing one wife justice vs many unfair, choosing halal dowry — following Allah's want turn.\n\nGreat deviation warning modern: media normalizing immorality.\n\nNext Allah wants to lighten for you.",
  "27": "Allah wants to lighten for you — humanity created weak.\n\nYuridu Allahu an yukhaffifa ankum wa khuliqa al-insanu da'ifa — Allah wants lighten — yukhaffif — ease.\n\nWa khuliqa al-insanu da'ifa — Humanity created weak — da'if — weak against desires (14 beautified loves), weak need companionship, weak need guidance.\n\nLightening shown in rukhsah: marry slave if cannot afford free, half punishment for slave when married, permission two three four but if fear injustice one, marry other women, give dowry willingly waive, test orphans not give wealth immediately, feed clothe speak kind.\n\nEase after detailed laws shows Shariah mercy not hardship — as earlier Allah intends ease not hardship (2:185), wants lighten.\n\nWeakness not insult but reality to seek strength via taqwa, patience, prayer, rope.\n\nRecognizing weak leads to tawakkul not arrogance.\n\nNext do not consume wealth among yourselves unjustly.",
  "28": "O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among yourselves unjustly except it be trade by mutual consent — do not kill yourselves — Allah Ever Merciful to you.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la ta'kulu amwalakum baynakum bil-batil illa an takuna tijaratan an taradin minkum — Do not consume wealth among yourselves unjustly — bil-batil — false, invalid — except trade by mutual consent — taradin — mutual pleasure.\n\nEarlier 2:188 do not consume wealth unjustly nor bring to judges to consume portion sinfully — same principle repeated for family wealth context.\n\nIlla trade mutual consent — tijarah — halal business with consent both parties, not coercion, not deception.\n\nWa la taqtulu anfusakum — Do not kill yourselves — could mean suicide, or killing one another as one family (as from single soul), or destroying yourselves via consuming wealth unjustly.\n\nInna Allaha kana bikum Rahima — Allah Merciful to you — forbids unjust consumption suicide killing because merciful.\n\nMutual consent trade shows economic justice.\n\nAfter weakening and lightening, wealth consumption rule important.\n\nNext whoever does that in aggression injustice.",
  "29": "Whoever does that in aggression and injustice — We will burn him in Fire — that for Allah is easy.\n\nWa man yaf'al dhalika udwanan wa zulman fa-sawfa nuslihi naran wa kana dhalika alalLahi yasira — Who does unjust consumption or killing selves in aggression injustice — udwan zulm — We will burn in Fire — easy for Allah.\n\nUdwan zulm — aggression injustice — same as those who retain wives to harm transgressing (2:231) wrongs self.\n\nEasy for Allah — yasira — not difficult.\n\nEarlier severe warning those consume orphan wealth eat Fire bellies blaze (10) — similar.\n\nWealth unjust consumption leads Fire.\n\nNext if avoid major sins small expiated.",
  "30": "If you avoid major sins you are forbidden, We will expiate your small sins and admit you to noble entrance.\n\nIn tajtanibu kaba'ira ma tunhawna anhu nukaffir ankum sayyi'atikum wa nudkhilakum mudkhalan karima — Avoid kaba'ir — major sins forbidden — adultery, consuming orphan wealth, riba, killing, associating, etc., We expiate small sins — sayyi'at — and admit noble entrance — mudkhal karim — honourable entry to Paradise, or noble place.\n\nMajor vs minor distinction: major has hadd punishment or curse or war declaration; minor less.\n\nAvoiding major shows taqwa, leads expiation minor.\n\nMudkhal karim — noble entrance — as earlier Gardens under rivers abiding forever great success.\n\nEncourages not despair minor slips if major avoided, but also not persist minor becomes major.\n\nNext do not wish what Allah favoured some with.",
  "31": "Do not wish for what Allah has favoured some of you over others — for men share of what they earned, women share of what they earned — ask Allah of His bounty — Allah Knowing of all.\n\nWa la tatamannaw ma faddala Allahu bihi ba'dakum ala ba'd — Do not wish — tatamannaw — envy what Allah favoured some over others — wealth, beauty, children, inheritance share male like two females, etc.\n\nLir-rijali nasibun mimma iktasabu wa lin-nisa nasibun mimma iktasabna — Men share what they earned, women share what they earned — nasib — share — earning includes work, effort. Envy not increase share; asking Allah increases.\n\nWas'alu Allaha min fadlih — Ask Allah of His bounty — fadl — as earlier bounty Owner great bounty (3:74) — ask from Him, not envy others.\n\nInnAllaha kana bi-kulli shay'in Alima — Knowing all — knows who deserves more, knows earning.\n\nAfter inheritance shares where male like two females some women might wish male share; verse says do not wish favoured others have, ask Allah of bounty.\n\nSame as earlier do not make Allah obstacle in oaths, do not follow steps Satan envy.\n\nFocus on own kasb — earning.\n\nNext for all We made heirs and those pledged.",
  "32": "For everyone We made heirs to what parents and relatives leave, and those whom your oaths pledged — give them share — Allah over all Witness.\n\nWa li-kullin ja'alna mawaliya mimma taraka al-walidan wal-aqrabun walladhina aqadat aymanukum fa-atuhum nasibahum — For everyone We made heirs — mawaliya — from what parents relatives leave — shares just described.\n\nWalladhina aqadat aymanukum — Those whom your oaths pledged — muwalah — alliance, brotherhood from Hijrah? They pledged mutual inheritance early Islam then abrogated but still give support.\n\nFa-atuhum nasibahum — Give share.\n\nInnAllaha kana ala kulli shay'in Shahidan — Allah Witness over all — Shahid — as earlier Allah Witness over what you do.\n\nHeirs made by Allah not by whim ensures fairness.\n\nOath pledged heirs shows honouring covenants.\n\nNext men qawwamun over women.",
  "33": "Men are maintainers of women by what Allah favoured some over others and by what they spend from wealth — righteous women devout guardians unseen as Allah guarded — those you fear rebellion admonish them, forsake beds, strike lightly — if obey seek no way against them — Allah Most High, Great.\n\nAr-rijalu qawwamuna ala an-nisa bima faddala Allahu ba'dahum ala ba'd wa bima anfaqu min amwalihim — Men maintainers women — qawwam — protector maintainer — by what Allah favoured some over others — physical strength, responsibility to provide, defend — and by spending wealth — mahr maintenance.\n\nFas-salihatu qanitatun hafizatun lil-ghayb bima hafiza Allah — Righteous women devout guardians of unseen as Allah guarded — preserve chastity wealth in husband absence as Allah preserved.\n\nWallati takhafuna nushuzahunna fa'izuhunna wahjuruhunna fil-madaji' wadribuhunna — Those fear nushuz — rebellion disobedience arrogance — admonish, forsake beds, strike — wadribu — lightly not harming, as last resort with conditions scholars detailed, not face, not severe, after failed admonition forsaking. Many scholars say striking symbolic with siwak not to harm; Prophet never struck wife.\n\nFa-in ata'nakum fa-la tabghu alayhinna sabila — If obey seek no way against them — no harm after obedience.\n\nInnAllaha kana Aliyyan Kabira — Most High Great — Aliyyan Kabiran — reminder to husbands who feel high over wives that Allah Higher Greater above them — if abuse, He Above.\n\nThis verse foundation qiwamah — responsibility not superiority. Maintainer spends, protects.\n\nNext if fear breach between two.",
  "34": "If you fear breach between them, send arbitrator from his family and from hers — if they desire reconciliation Allah will cause agreement — Allah Knowing, Aware.\n\nWa in khiftum shiqaqa baynihima fab'athu hakaman min ahlihi wa hakaman min ahliha in yurida islahan yuwaffiq Allahu baynahuma — If fear breach shiqaq — rupture — between couple, send hakam arbitrator from his family and hers — family understands background.\n\nIn yurida islahan yuwaffiq Allahu baynahuma — If both arbitrators desire reconciliation Allah will cause agreement success — tawfiq — from Allah.\n\nInnAllaha kana Aliman Khabira — Knowing Aware — knows intention reconciliation or not.\n\nThis provides mediation before divorce, involves families, seeks islah — same root as correcting between them (2:182) and setting right orphans (2:220) and brothers.\n\nShiqaq — rift — as earlier schism (3:105) division after clear proofs — similar within family.\n\nFamily arbitration maintains privacy, dignity.\n\nFor today counselling: involve trustworthy family who want reconciliation not spread gossip.\n\nNext worship Allah associate none.",
  "35": "Worship Allah and associate none with Him — be good to parents, relatives, orphans, needy, near neighbour, far neighbour, companion at side, traveler, what right hands possess — Allah does not love arrogant boastful.\n\nWa'budu Allaha wa la tushriku bihi shay'an wa bil-walidayni ihsanan wa bidhi al-qurba wal-yatama wal-masakin wal-jari dhi al-qurba wal-jari al-junub was-sahibi bil-janbi wabni as-sabil wa ma malakat aymanukum — Worship Allah associate none — tawhid — then ihsan to layers: parents, relatives, orphans, needy, near neighbour — qurb — far neighbour — junub — companion side — Sahib — friend, spouse, colleague travelling, traveler, slaves what right hands possess.\n\nInnAllaha la yuhibbu man kana mukhtalan fakhura — Allah does not love arrogant boastful — mukhtal fakhur — arrogant boastful about wealth lineage, looks down others, opposite ihsan.\n\nThis verse comprehensive social map: after family arbitration, extends to community: parents top, then relatives, orphans, needy, neighbours near far, companion, traveler, slaves — all you interact.\n\nTawhid grounds ihsan; without worship Allah, ihsan shallow.\n\nAllah does not love arrogant boastful — as earlier not love transgressors, not love corruption.\n\nNext those who are stingy enjoin stinginess conceal bounty.",
  "36": "Those who are stingy and enjoin people to be stingy and hide what Allah gave them of bounty — We prepared for disbelievers humiliating punishment.\n\nAlladhina yabkhaluna wa ya'muruna an-nasa bil-bukhli wa yaktumuna ma atahumu Allahu min fadlih — Those stingy — yabkhaluna — and enjoin people stinginess and hide bounty — yaktumuna — conceal — as earlier People Book hide Book for small price, hide description.\n\nWa a'tadna lil-kafirina adhaban muhina — Prepared for disbelievers humiliating punishment — muhin — humiliating.\n\nBukhl — stinginess — opposite spending beloved (3:92) spending ease hardship (3:134) spending night day (2:274) and asking Allah of bounty (31). Concealing bounty is like hiding Book covenant not making clear (3:187).\n\nMukhtal fakhur arrogant boastful (35) often stingy.\n\nPrepared humiliating punishment.\n\nNext those spend to show people not believe Allah Last Day — Satan companion evil.",
  "37": "And those who spend wealth to show people and do not believe in Allah nor Last Day — whose companion is Satan — evil companion.\n\nWalladhina yunfiquna amwalahum ri'a an-nasi wa la yu'minuna billahi wa la bil-yawmi al-akhir wa man yakun ash-Shaytanu lahu qarinan fa-sa'a qarin — Those spend to show people riya — and not believe Allah Last Day — whose companion Satan evil companion — qarin.\n\nRiya spending as earlier blotted like dust on smooth rock rain leaves bare (2:264). Not believe — motive not Allah pleasure.\n\nCompanion Satan — qarin — as earlier Satan threatens poverty orders immorality (2:268) tries make fear his allies (3:175). Evil companion leads.\n\nEarlier stingy and enjoin stingy bad, riya spending also bad — extremes: withholding and showing off both condemned; middle: spend seeking Allah pleasure certainty from within (2:265) garden high ground.\n\nNext what harm if believed spent?",
  "38": "What harm would be on them if they believed in Allah and Last Day and spent from what Allah provided? Allah Knowing of them.\n\nWa ma dha alayhim law amanu billahi wal-yawmi al-akhir wa anfaqu mimma razaqahum Allah wa kan Allahu bihim Alima — What harm would be on them if believed and spent from what Allah provided? Ma dha alayhim — what harm — i.e., no harm, rather benefit.\n\nIf believed Last Day spent from provision — razaqahum — as earlier taste we provided (2:57) etc — gain Gardens, ridwan, forgiveness.\n\nAllah Knowing of them — Alim — knows who stingy, who riya, who believes spends — as earlier Seeing, Knowing appears around spending.\n\nEncourages: believing spending no harm; withholding riya harm.\n\nNext Allah does not wrong atom's weight.",
  "39": "Indeed Allah does not wrong weight of atom — if good He multiplies and gives from Himself great reward.\n\nInna Allaha la yazlimu mithqala dharratin wa in taku hasanatan yuda'ifha wa yu'ti min ladunhu ajran azima — Does not wrong weight atom — mithqala dharratin — smallest ant? Atom — smallest weight.\n\nIf good multiplies — yuda'if — and gives from Himself great reward — ajr azim — same as great reward responded after injury (3:177) and great bounty Owner great bounty (3:74).\n\nThis after spending discussion: Allah not wrong atom; spending beloved, spending ease hardship not lost; withholding, riya not ignorable.\n\nAtom weight justice ensures every deed counted.\n\nGreat reward from Himself shows bounty beyond multiplication.\n\nNext how when We bring witness from every nation.",
  "40": "How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as witness over these? Fa-kayfa idha ji'na min kulli ummatin bi-shahidin wa ji'na bika ala ha'ula'i shahida — How will it be when brought from every nation witness — prophet of nation — and bring you Muhammad as witness over these — your nation or over all witnesses — shahida.\n\nWitnesses bring on Day — testimony as earlier best nation witnesses over humanity and Messenger witness over you (2:143).\n\nHow will it be — kayfa — leaves imagination — horror for those who twisted, hope for those who believed.\n\nThis verse after atom weight justice: witnesses testify atom weight deeds.\n\nBelievers fear day.\n\nNext those disbelieved wish earth levelled.",
  "41": "That Day those disbelieved and disobeyed Messenger will wish they were levelled with earth — they will not hide any statement from Allah.\n\nYawma'idhin yawaddu alladhina kafaru wa asaw ar-Rasula law tusawwa bihim al-ardu wa la yaktumuna Allaha hadithan — Day those disbelieved disobeyed Messenger wish were levelled with earth — tusawwa bihim al-ard — flattened — so earth over them, hidden, not exposed.\n\nWa la yaktumuna Allaha hadithan — Will not hide any statement from Allah — as earlier conceal reveal Allah knows (3:29), nothing hidden, qawl conceal, but Day cannot hide.\n\nWish levelled shows terror.\n\nFor believers, opposite wish: present good present, not wish distance.\n\nNext do not approach prayer while intoxicated until know what saying nor in state impurity except passing.",
  "42": "O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say nor in impurity except passing through — until you bathe — if ill or on journey or one came from privy or touched women and find no water, then dry ablution with clean earth — wipe faces and hands — Allah Ever Pardoning, Forgiving.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la taqrabu as-salata wa antum sukara hatta ta'lamu ma taquluna wa la junuban illa abiri sabil hatta taghtasilu — Do not approach prayer intoxicated until know what saying — early prohibition before total wine ban — gradual, as earlier wine gambling great sin benefit greater sin (2:219).\n\nNor junub — impurity after intercourse — except passing through mosque — abiri sabil — until bathe — ghusl.\n\nWa in kuntum marda aw ala safarin aw ja'a ahadukum min al-gha'it aw lamastum an-nisa fa-lam tajidu ma'an fa-tayammamu sa'idan tayyiban famsahu bi-wujuhikum wa aydikum — If ill, journey, came from privy, touched women — lamastum — intercourse? — find no water then tayammum clean earth wipe faces hands.\n\nInnAllaha kana Afuwwan Ghafuran — Ever Pardoning Forgiving — pardons past approaching prayer intoxicated before full prohibition.\n\nTayammum ease — as earlier Allah intends ease not hardship (2:185), wants lighten (27).\n\nShows prayer guarded even ill journey, but concession clean earth.\n\nNext have you not seen those given portion Scripture purchasing error.",
  "43": "Have you not seen those given portion of Scripture purchasing error and wishing you stray from path? They purchase error and wish you stray.\n\nAlam tara ila alladhina utu nasiban min al-Kitab yashtaruna ad-dalalata wa yuriduna an tadillu as-sabil — Given portion Book purchase error — yashtaruna ad-dalalata — as earlier those purchased error with guidance trade no profit (2:16) and sold souls magic (2:102).\n\nYuriduna an tadillu as-sabil — Want you stray path — as earlier wish mislead you (3:69) wish turn you back after belief (2:109).\n\nPortion — nasib — again not whole.\n\nPurchasing error — buying misguidance with guidance, paying price.\n\nWishing you stray — active desire not passive.\n\nNext Allah knows your enemies sufficient Allah as Wali sufficient Allah as Helper.",
  "44": "Allah knows your enemies — sufficient Allah as Guardian, sufficient Allah as Helper. Wallahu A'lamu bi-a'da'ikum wa kafa billahi Waliyyan wa kafa billahi Nasira — Allah knows your enemies — A'lam — Knows deception morning-evening plot, twisting tongues, stinginess.\n\nKafa billahi Waliyyan wa kafa billahi Nasira — Sufficient Allah as Guardian sufficient Helper — same as Allah is your Guardian best Helper (3:150). If enemies many, sufficiency Allah enough.\n\nWali — Guardian as earlier Allah Guardian believers brings darkness light (2:257). Nasir — Helper as earlier best Helper.\n\nIf Allah sufficient, no need take bitanah outside or awliya instead of believers.\n\nNext among Jews who distort words from places.",
  "45": "Among Jews are those who distort words from places and say we hear and disobey and hear — may you not hear — and ra'ina — twisting tongues and stabbing religion — if they said we hear and obey and hear and look upon us it would be better and upright.\n\nMin alladhina hadu yuharrifuna al-kalima an mawadi'ihi wa yaquluna sami'na wa asayna wasma' ghayra musma'in wa ra'ina layyan bi-alsinatihim wa ta'nan fid-din — Among Jews distort words from places — yuharrifuna — shifting meaning, as earlier twisting Book with tongues (3:78) and distorting words from places (5:13).\n\nSami'na wa asayna — We hear and disobey — opposite we hear obey (2:285, 3:53). Wasma' ghayra musma' — Hear may you not hear — cursing Prophet. Ra'ina — with twist as earlier Do not say Ra'ina say Unzurna (2:104) — exploited double meaning.\n\nLayyan bi-alsinatihim wa ta'nan fid-din — Twisting tongues stabbing religion.\n\nWa law annahum qalu sami'na wa ata'na wasma' wanzurna lakana khayran lahum wa aqwam — If said we hear obey and hear and look upon us better upright — aqwam — more upright.\n\nWa lakin la'anahum Allahu bi-kufrihim fa-la yu'minuna illa qalilan — But Allah cursed them for disbelief so believe only little.\n\nCurse due disbelief, distortion.\n\nNext People Book believe in what We sent down confirming.",
  "46": "O People of Book, believe in what We sent down confirming what with you before We efface faces and turn them to backs or curse them as We cursed Sabbath people — command Allah done.\n\nYa Ahla al-Kitab aminu bima nazzalna musaddiqan lima ma'akum min qabli an natmisa wujuhan fa-naruddaha ala adbariha aw nal'anahum kama la'anna Ashab as-Sabt — Believe what We sent down confirming what with you — same as Quran confirming.\n\nBefore We efface faces turn to backs — natmisa — efface features — turn them to backs — or curse as Sabbath companions — Ashab as-Sabt turned monkeys for breaking Sabbath.\n\nWa kana amru Allahi maf'ula — Command Allah done — when decrees Be.\n\nSevere warning: effacing faces turning backs — literal? Metaphor for humiliation.\n\nAfter distortion ra'ina, now warning curse as Sabbath.\n\nInvitation still believe before efface.\n\nNext Allah does not forgive shirk forgives less than that.",
  "47": "Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners associated with Him but forgives less than that for whom He wills — whoever associates with Allah has fabricated great sin.\n\nInna Allaha la yaghfiru an yushraka bihi wa yaghfiru ma duna dhalika liman yasha wa man yushrik billahi fa-qad iftara ithman azima — Allah does not forgive shirk — an yushraka bihi — if dies upon shirk without repentance.\n\nBut forgives less than that — ma duna dhalika — minor major sins besides shirk — for whom wills — by His mercy.\n\nMan yushrik fa-qad iftara ithman azima — Whoever associates fabricated great sin — iftira ithm azim — similar fabricated lie about Allah after brought Torah (3:94).\n\nShirk not forgiven if died upon — greatest wrong.\n\nBut less than shirk forgiven — hope for sinners.\n\nLinks earlier Allah does not love those take deities? Actually earlier Allah is One God no partners (2:163, 3:2).\n\nNext those who purify themselves.",
  "48": "Have you not seen those who claim purity for themselves — Allah purifies whom He wills — they will not be wronged a thread.\n\nAlam tara ila alladhina yuzakkuna anfusahum — See those who claim purity selves — yuzakkuna anfusahum — claim we pure, best, exclusive Paradise (2:111), Fire few days (2:80,3:24).\n\nBal Allahu yuzakki man yasha — But Allah purifies whom wills — yuzakki — purification from Him not self claim.\n\nWa la yuzlamuna fatila — Not wronged even thread — fatil — tiny filament date seed — atom weight justice (39) not wrong even tiny.\n\nSelf-purification claim arrogance opposite muttaqin who seek forgiveness dawn (17) see excess seek forgiveness.\n\nNext look how they fabricate lies.",
  "49": "Look how they fabricate lies about Allah — sufficient as a clear sin. Unzur kayfa yaftaruna ala Allahi al-kadhiba wa kafa bihi ithman mubina — Look how they fabricate lies — yaftaruna al-kadhiba — lie about Allah — saying Allah is poor and we are rich (3:181), saying Isa is Allah (5:17), saying Messiah third of three (5:110), claiming Allah commanded not to believe unless offering consumed by fire (3:183), claiming no blame concerning unlettered (3:75), claiming Fire will touch only few days (2:80, 3:24).\n\nWa kafa bihi ithman mubina — sufficient as clear sin — ithm mubin — open, manifest sin. Why sufficient? Because lie about Allah corrupts source of guidance; if source corrupted, all branches corrupted. Fabricating small prohibition and ascribing to Allah adds burden to people and removes mercy intended to lighten (27).\n\nFor us, caution: saying \"Islam says\" without knowledge is fabrication. Prophet warned whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take seat in Fire. How much more lying about Allah?\n\nNext they believe in false gods Taghut and say disbelievers more guided than believers — layer of fabrication: inventing gods besides Allah, then ranking disbelievers above believers.",
  "50": "Have you not seen those given portion Scripture believe in false gods and taghut and say about disbelievers they more guided than believers? Believe in jibt and taghut — false gods — and say about disbelievers polytheists more guided than believers — referring to Quraysh? Jews told Quraysh more guided than Muslims to please Quraysh.\n\nJibt and taghut — idols, sorcery, false deities, tyrants.\n\nSaying disbelievers more guided than believers — inverted guidance — envious after truth clear (2:109) wish turn back, envy.\n\nThis corruption due deviation after knowledge (3:19).\n\nNext those cursed Allah.",
  "51": "Those cursed by Allah — whoever Allah curses you will find no helper. Ula'ika alladhina la'anahum Allahu wa man yal'ani Allahu fa-lan tajida lahu nasira — Those cursed — la'nahum — expelled from mercy for believing in jibt and taghut — false idols, tyrants, sorcery — and saying disbelievers more guided than believers to please polytheists.\n\nWa man yal'ani Allahu fa-lan tajida lahu nasira — Whoever Allah curses will find no helper — nasir — no protector — same as earlier fuel Fire no helpers (3:10), deeds wasted no helpers (3:22), those disbelieved severe punishment no helpers (4:56). Cursed means cut off from mercy; who can reconnect?\n\nCurse due to choosing guidance inverted: they had portion Scripture (50), given knowledge, but believed in false gods and said disbelievers more guided — inversion of Furqan (2:185) that distinguishes right wrong. Instead of using knowledge to distinguish, they inverted.\n\nFor believer, lesson about alliance: those cursed sought alliance with disbelievers claiming they more guided, seeking honour — honour belongs Allah entirely (4:127-139). Seeking honour with cursed brings curse.\n\nNext do they have share of dominion? If so they would not give people even speck — stinginess of cursed.",
  "52": "Or do they have share of dominion? If so they would not give people even speck.\n\nAm lahum nasibun min al-mulk fa-idhan la yu'tuna an-nasa naqira — Do they have share dominion? Mulk — dominion Owner (3:26) gives whom wills. If they had share, would not give people even naqir — speck on date seed — tiny.\n\nNaqir — smallest spot — shows stinginess.\n\nThose who said disbelievers more guided than believers if had dominion would be stingy, not generous.\n\nOpposite Allah Owner great bounty (3:74) provides without account.\n\nThis exposes envy: they wish not receive any blessing (2:105) would not give speck.\n\nNext envy people for what Allah gave of bounty.",
  "53": "Or do they envy people for what Allah gave them of bounty? We gave family Ibrahim Book and wisdom and great kingdom.\n\nAm yahsuduna an-nasa ala ma atahumu Allahu min fadlih — Envy people for what Allah gave bounty — hasad — same as many among People Book wish turn you back envy after truth clear (2:109, 3:69), envy for mercy chosen (2:105).\n\nFa-qad atayna Ala Ibrahima al-Kitaba wal-hikmata wa ataynahum mulkan azima — We gave family Ibrahim Book wisdom great kingdom — Dawud Sulaiman kingdom vast.\n\nIf gave Ibrahim family Book wisdom kingdom, giving Muhammad similar not strange.\n\nEnvy stems from bounty Owner.\n\nNext some believed some turned away — Hell sufficient blaze.",
  "54": "Some believed in him and some turned away — Hell sufficient as Blaze. Fa-minhum man amana bihi wa minhum man sadda anhu wa kafa bi-Jahannam sa'ira — Some believed in him — in whom? In Ibrahim family? In Prophet Muhammad? In family of Ibrahim given Book wisdom great kingdom (53)? Some believed, some turned away — sadda — blocked, turned away.\n\nWa kafa bi-Jahannam sa'ira — Hell sufficient as Blaze — sa'ir — blazing fire — enough as recompense.\n\nThis pattern repeats throughout: after envy for bounty Owner great bounty, some believe some turn away. Same with Isa: some believed (hawariyyun) some said Allah is Messiah, third of three.\n\nBelief vs turning away choice after envy, after clear proofs.\n\nHell sufficient Blaze — not needing additional torture — its heat, depth, eternity sufficient.\n\nFor us, question: am I among who believed or who turned away after knowledge came out of jealousy?\n\nAfter this, severe warning for those disbelieved Our signs We will burn in Fire whenever skins matured replaced — to taste punishment.\n\nNext skins replaced to taste.",
  "55": "Those who disbelieved Our signs — We will burn them in Fire — whenever skins matured We replace with other skins to taste punishment — Allah Mighty, Wise.\n\nInna alladhina kafaru bi-ayatina sawfa nuslihim naran kullama nadijat juluduhum baddalnahum juludan ghayraha li-yadhuqu al-adhab — Burn Fire, skins matured — nadijat — cooked — replaced other skins to taste punishment — continuous.\n\nInnAllaha kana Azizan Hakima — Mighty Wise — Mighty to punish, Wise placement.\n\nSigns disbelieved includes Torah Injil Quran, Isa birth, first House.\n\nTaste punishment — dhawq — as earlier taste Fire (2:211?), taste punishment burning (3:181).\n\nFor believer protection from Fire better than beautified desires.\n\nNext believers righteous admitted Gardens.",
  "56": "Those who believed and did righteous deeds — We will admit them Gardens under which rivers flow abiding forever — therein purified spouses — admit to abundant shade.\n\nWalladhina amanu wa amilu as-salihat sa-nudkhiluhum jannatin tajri min tahtiha al-anhar khalidina fiha abadan lahum fiha azwajun mutahharah wa nudkhiluhum zillan zalila — Gardens rivers eternal, purified spouses mutahharah, shade abundant — zillan zalilan — deep shade.\n\nOpposite previous Fire skins replaced, here Gardens eternal purified spouses not like stepmothers inherited.\n\nMutahharah — purified from defects as earlier pure spouses Paradise (3:15).\n\nZillan zalilan — shade — not scorching sun.\n\nPromise for believers righteous.\n\nNext Allah commands return trusts to owners and judge with justice.",
  "57": "Allah commands you return trusts to owners and when you judge between people judge with justice — excellent admonition Allah exhorts you — Allah Hearing, Seeing.\n\nInna Allaha ya'murukum an tu'addu al-amanati ila ahliha wa idha hakamtum bayna an-nasi an tahkumu bil-adl — Return trusts — amanat — to owners — includes orphan wealth, dowry, testimony, leadership, etc.\n\nWhen judge between people judge with justice — adl.\n\nInna Allaha ni'imma ya'izukum bih — Excellent admonition.\n\nInnAllaha kana Sami'an Basira — Hearing, Seeing — hears trusts returned, sees justice.\n\nAmanah and adl two pillars society after family.\n\nEarlier not consume wealth unjustly (28-29), give orphans wealth (2), return trusts now.\n\nJustice includes inheritance shares, marriage justice (33-34 qiwamah).\n\nNext obey Allah and Messenger and those in authority among you.",
  "58": "O you who believe, obey Allah and obey Messenger and those in authority among you — if you dispute about anything return it to Allah and Messenger if you believe in Allah Last Day — that better and more excellent interpretation.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu ati'u Allaha wa ati'u ar-Rasula wa uli al-amri minkum — Obey Allah, Messenger, those in authority among you — uli al-amr — scholars, leaders, parents? Among you — meaning Muslims? Or just.\n\nFa-in tanaza'tum fi shay'in fa-rudduhu ila Allahi war-Rasuli in kuntum tu'minuna billahi wal-yawmi al-akhir — If dispute anything return to Allah and Messenger — Quran Sunnah — if believe Allah Last Day.\n\nDhalika khayrun wa ahsanu ta'wilan — Better and more excellent interpretation — ta'wil — outcome.\n\nObedience three levels: Allah, Messenger, authority. Authority obedience conditional not disobey Allah? Prophet said no obedience creature in disobedience Creator.\n\nReturn dispute to Allah Messenger shows Quran Sunnah criterion — Furqan.\n\nEarlier common word, rope, now return to Allah Messenger.\n\nBest interpretation — ta'wil — as earlier deviant hearts follow mutashabih seeking discord seeking ta'wil (3:7) — proper ta'wil returns to Allah Messenger.\n\nNext those claim believe what revealed to you and before want go to taghut.",
  "59": "Have you not seen those who claim to believe in what was revealed to you and what revealed before you — want to go to taghut for judgment while commanded to disbelieve in it — Satan wants to lead them far astray.\n\nAlam tara ila alladhina yaz'umuna annahum amanu bima unzila ilayka wa ma unzila min qablika yuriduna an yatahakamu ila at-taghut wa qad umiru an yakfuru bihi wa yuridu Ash-Shaytanu an yudillahum dalalan ba'idan — Claim believe what revealed to you and before but want judgment to taghut — false judge, tyrant, law other than Allah — while commanded to disbelieve taghut — earlier disbelieve taghut and believe Allah grasps firm handhold (2:256).\n\nSatan wants lead far astray — dalalan ba'idan — far.\n\nClaim belief but preference taghut judgment reveals insincerity — as earlier wish mislead, twisting.\n\nHistorical: Jew and hypocrite dispute went to Ka'b ibn Ashraf? Or Prophet but hypocrite wanted Jewish judge because bribe?\n\nTrue belief requires disbelieve taghut.\n\nNext when told come to what Allah revealed and Messenger they see hypocrites turn away.",
  "60": "When told, Come to what Allah revealed and to Messenger, you see hypocrites turning away with aversion.\n\nWa idha qila lahum ta'alaw ila ma anzala Allahu wa ila ar-Rasuli ra'ayta al-munafiqina yasudduna anka sududa — When told come to what Allah revealed and Messenger, hypocrites turn away with aversion — sududa — blocking aversion.\n\nSame pattern as People given portion Scripture invited Book Allah to judge between them group turns away (3:23) and People Book why disbelieve signs while Allah Witness.\n\nHypocrites claim belief but when invited to Quran Sunnah to settle, turn away aversion.\n\nYasudduna anka sududa — turn away blocking — as earlier avert from path those believe seeking crooked (3:99).\n\nNext how when affliction strikes due to what hands sent forth then come swearing we intended only good.",
  "61": "How will it be when affliction strikes them for what hands sent forth then they come to you swearing By Allah we intended only good and reconciliation?\n\nFa-kayfa idha asabat-hum musibatun bima qaddamat aydihim thumma ja'uka yahlifuna billahi in aradna illa ihsanan wa tawfiqa — When affliction — musibah — due to what hands sent forth — earlier neglect — then come swearing we intended only good reconciliation — ihsan tawfiq — same words as arbitrators desire reconciliation Allah will cause agreement (34) — but hypocrites use as cover.\n\nThey swear By Allah.\n\nEarlier those with pleasing speech call Allah witness what in heart yet most quarrelsome opponent (2:204).\n\nHow will it be — kayfa — leaves imagination — distress.\n\nNext those Allah knows what in hearts so turn away admonish them speak to them penetrating words.",
  "62": "Those — Allah knows what is in hearts — so turn away from them, admonish them, and say to them about themselves penetrating words.\n\nUla'ika alladhina ya'lamu Allahu ma fi qulubihim fa-a'rid anhum wa 'izhum wa qul lahum fi anfusihim qawlan balighan — Those Allah knows what hearts — Allah knows conceal reveal (29) knows what chests conceal greater (118).\n\nTurn away from them — a'rid — not take as inner circle (116) — admonish — 'iz — exhort — and say about themselves penetrating words — qawlan balighan — reaching, impactful, about themselves — private confronting.\n\nThree steps: turn away politically, admonish publicly? Actually admonish, and private penetrating about selves — perhaps because hypocrites hide; words about selves penetrate.\n\nQawlan balighan — as earlier qawlan ma'rufan kind, qawlan sadida right, qawlan balighan penetrating.\n\nFor leader dealing with hypocrites: not all public shaming, sometimes turn away, sometimes admonish, sometimes private penetrative talk to reach heart.\n\nNext We did not send messenger except to be obeyed by permission Allah.",
  "63": "We did not send any messenger except to be obeyed by Allah's permission — had they when wronged themselves come to you seeking forgiveness and Messenger sought forgiveness — they would have found Allah Accepting repentance Merciful.\n\nWa ma arsalna min rasulin illa li-yuta'a bi-idhni Allah — No messenger sent except to be obeyed by permission Allah — not merely inform but obeyed — yuta' — same as obey Allah Messenger (58).\n\nWa law annahum idh zalamu anfusahum ja'uka fastaghfaru Allaha wastaghfara lahum ar-Rasulu la-wajadu Allaha Tawwaba Rahima — Had they when wronged selves come to you seeking forgiveness Allah and Messenger sought forgiveness — they'd find Allah Accepting Merciful.\n\nThis verse foundation seeking intercession through Messenger? Scholars discuss: coming to Prophet while alive, or after? Majority say coming to him while alive for istighfar. And general repentance seeking forgiveness via Prophet dua.\n\nLike earlier those who concealed came? Door open: come, seek forgiveness, Messenger seeks forgiveness.\n\nTawwaba Rahima — Accepting Merciful.\n\nHypocrites instead turn away aversion; had they come, found mercy.\n\nNext not by your Lord they will not believe until make you judge.",
  "64": "No, by your Lord they will not believe until they make you judge in what is disputed between them then find no discomfort in selves from what you judged and submit fully.\n\nFala wa Rabbika la yu'minuna hatta yuhakkimuka fi-ma shajara baynahum thumma la yajidu fi anfusihim harajan mimma qadayta wa yusallimu taslima — No by Lord they not believe until make you judge in disputes — shajara — that occurs between them — then find no haraj — discomfort — in selves from what you judged and submit fully — taslima — total submission.\n\nThis verse defines iman not just claim but acceptance of Prophet judgment.\n\nYuhakkimuka — make you judge — as earlier return dispute to Allah Messenger if believe.\n\nHaraj — discomfort resistance — in chest — as earlier (3:118) hatred appeared mouths what chests conceal greater — this chest discomfort about judgment.\n\nYusallimu taslima — submit fully — as earlier aslamtu submission (3:20).\n\nNo by Lord oath — Fala wa Rabbika — emphasizes by Lord.\n\nFaith requires three: make him judge, find no discomfort, submit fully.\n\nFor today, Sunnah judgment not only Quran.\n\nNext had We decreed upon them kill yourselves or leave homes only few would do.",
  "65": "Had We decreed upon them kill yourselves or leave your homes — only few would do — had they done what exhorted, better and more strengthening.\n\nWa law annā katabna alayhim an iqtulu anfusakum aw ikhruju min diyarikum ma fa'aluhu illa qalilun minhum — Had decreed kill selves or leave homes — like Bani Israel were told kill selves after calf (2:54) and leave Egypt — only few would do.\n\nWa law annahum fa'alu ma yu'azuna bihi lakana khayran lahum wa ashadda tathbita — Had they done what exhorted — obedience Messenger (58) etc — better and more strengthening — tathbita — firm.\n\nShows human weakness — humanity created weak (27) — decreed harsh only few do. But what actually exhorted gentle: obey, return trusts, justice, not consume wealth unjustly, spend beloved — doable.\n\nBetter and stronger if done.\n\nNext whoever obeys Allah and Messenger those with those Allah blessed.",
  "66": "Whoever obeys Allah and Messenger — they will be with those Allah blessed — among prophets, truthful, martyrs, righteous — excellent companions.\n\nWa man yuti'i Allaha war-Rasula fa-ula'ika ma'a alladhina an'ama Allahu alayhim min an-nabiyyina was-siddiqina wash-shuhada was-salihina wa hasuna ula'ika rafiqa — Who obeys Allah Messenger with those Allah blessed — an'ama — favour earlier manna upon believers raising messenger (3:164).\n\nAmong prophets, siddiqin — truthful — shuhada — martyrs witnesses — salihin — righteous — categories.\n\nWa hasuna ula'ika rafiqa — Excellent companions — rafiq — companion.\n\nThis verse hope after obedience: companionship high.\n\nRafiq — companion — as later companion at side (36) but supreme companions.\n\nObedience leads to being with blessed, not necessarily becoming prophet but with them in Paradise — as per hadith man loves people will be with them.\n\nNext favour from Allah sufficient Knower.",
  "67": "That bounty is from Allah — sufficient is Allah as Knower. Dhalika al-fadlu min Allah wa kafa billahi Alima — That favour — being with those Allah blessed among prophets, truthful, martyrs, righteous excellent companions (66) — is from Allah — not earned alone — fadl — bounty — Owner great bounty (3:74, 3:174), great bounty for believers who responded after injury etc.\n\nWa kafa billahi Alima — Sufficient Allah as Knower — Knower who obeys, who deserves companionship, who strives wealth selves, who empathizes weak offspring fear, who returns trusts, judges justice.\n\nAlim appears around obedience to Prophet, around atom weight justice (39-40) — Knower of deeds atom weight.\n\nSufficient Knower means He knows who sincerely obeys Allah Messenger vs who claims belief but wants taghut judgment, turns away aversion (59-60).\n\nSo bounty being with blessed is from Allah, and He knows who deserves.\n\nNext take precautions go forth groups or all together — preparation after knowing reward.\n\nThis verse closes section about obedience leading to excellent companions — favour from Allah, Knower suffices.\n\nPractical: do not seek validation people for being with blessed; Allah knows.\n\nNext take precautions.",
  "68": "O you who believe, take your precautions and go forth in groups or all together.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu khudhu hizrakum fanfiru thubatin aw infiru jami'an — Take precautions — hizr — Guard, preparation, arms, planning — then go forth — fanfiru — mobilize — thubatin — groups — or all together — jami'an.\n\nAfter spiritual preparation obedience, companionship, now physical preparation.\n\nTake precautions — hizr — as earlier take provisions best provision taqwa (2:197) — physical and spiritual.\n\nGo forth groups or all — depending need.\n\nEncourages readiness balanced with tawakkul — earlier Allah sufficient Guardian Helper, but take precautions ordered.\n\nNext among you is one who lags behind.",
  "69": "Among you is one who lags behind — if affliction strikes you he says Allah favoured me not being present with them — if bounty from Allah reaches you he says — as if no affection between you — would that I were with them so I achieve great success.\n\nWa inna minkum la-man layubatti'anna — Among you who lags — yubatti' — slow, discourages.\n\nFa-in asabatkum musibatun qala qad an'ama Allahu alayya idh lam akun ma'ahum shahida — If affliction strikes you says Allah favoured me not present witness — relief not helping.\n\nWa la-in asabakum fadlun min Allah la-yaqulanna ka-an lam takun baynakum wa baynahu mawaddatun ya laytani kuntu ma'ahum fa-afuza fawzan azima — If bounty reaches you says as if no affection between you — would that I were with them achieve great success — fawz azim — great success — but success defined as bounty worldly gain, not forgiveness mercy better than accumulation (3:157).\n\nLayubatti' — lingerer — hypocrite who slows others, opposite those race good deeds (3:114).\n\nAs if no affection — mawaddah — shows hypocrite loves not believers despite claim.\n\nGreat success — fawz azim — same phrase used for Paradise success earlier.\n\nFor this hypocrite fawz azim is spoils; for believer Gardens great success.\n\nNext let fight in Allah path those sell worldly life for Hereafter.",
  "70": "So let those fight in Allah's path who sell worldly life for Hereafter — whoever fights then killed or overcomes We will give great reward.\n\nFalyuqatil fi sabili Allahi alladhina yashruna al-hayata ad-dunya bil-akhirah — Let fight path Allah those sell worldly life for Hereafter — yashruna — sell worldly for Hereafter — opposite those sell Hereafter for worldly for small price — earlier.\n\nWa man yuqatil fi sabili Allahi fa-yuqtal aw yaghlib fa-sawfa nu'tihi ajran azima — Who fights killed or overcomes give great reward — ajr azim — same as great success but ajr azim — great reward — whether killed or overcomes both rewarded because intention sale.\n\nShows two outcomes both success: killed martyrdom alive with Lord provided, overcomes returns favour bounty no harm (3:179) both great reward.\n\nFor lukewarm lagger (69) who calculates worldly success, contrast person who sold worldly for Hereafter — regardless outcome wins.\n\nConnection to earlier spend from what love (3:92) — selling worldly.\n\nNext what is wrong with you that you do not fight for weak among men women children.",
  "71": "What is wrong with you that you do not fight for weak among men women children who say Our Lord take us out of this town whose people are oppressors and appoint for us from Yourself guardian and helper?\n\nWa ma lakum la tuqatiluna fi sabili Allahi wal-mustad'afina min ar-rijali wan-nisa wal-wildani alladhina yaquluna Rabbana akhrijna... — What wrong you not fight for weak — mustad'afin — among men women children who say Our Lord take us out town whose people oppressors and appoint for us from Yourself guardian helper.\n\nEarlier (2:243) those fled homes thousands fearing death; here weak who cannot flee calling dua for guardian helper — mustad'afina — oppressed.\n\nFighting cause weak, not for dominance — defensive to protect weak who pray for rescue.\n\nDua weak: akhrijna min hadhihi al-qaryah az-zalimu ahluha waj'al lana min ladunka waliyyan waj'al lana min ladunka nasira — Take us out town oppressors people appoint for us from Yourself guardian helper — similar to Allah knows enemies sufficient Allah as Wali Nasir (44).\n\nThis verse basis for humanitarian intervention — fighting to rescue oppressed.\n\nIf you have strength and weak calling, what is wrong you not fight?\n\nNext those who believed fight in Allah path those disbelieved fight in Taghut path so fight allies Satan.\n\nAfter call fight for weak, next verses continue...",
  "72": "Those who believed fight in Allah's path and those who disbelieved fight in Taghut path — so fight allies of Satan — Satan's plot ever weak.\n\nAlladhina amanu yuqatiluna fi sabili Allah walladhina kafaru yuqatiluna fi sabili at-taghut fa-qatilu awliya ash-Shaytan inna kayda ash-Shaytani kana da'ifa — Those believed fight path Allah, disbelieved fight path Taghut — Taghut false gods tyrants as earlier disbelieve Taghut believe Allah grasps firm handhold (2:256), guardians Taghut bring light to darkness (2:257).\n\nSo fight allies Satan — awliya ash-Shaytan.\n\nInn Kayda ash-Shaytani kana da'ifa — Satan's plot ever weak — da'if — weak — compared plot Allah best planners (3:54). Threatens poverty, tries make fear allies (3:175), but weak.\n\nTwo paths: Allah path vs Taghut path — as earlier Islam Way vs other, Allah Guardian vs Taghut guardians.\n\nFight allies Satan because they fight for oppression weak.\n\nPlot weak — so need not fear them fear Me (3:175).\n\nEncouragement after not fight for weak?\n\nNext have you not seen those told restrain hands establish prayer give zakah but when fighting prescribed group feared people as fear Allah or more.",
  "73": "Have you not seen those who were told restrain hands, establish prayer, give zakah — but when fighting prescribed, group among them fear people as fear Allah or more and said Our Lord why prescribed fighting upon us — if only You delayed us short term — Say enjoyment world little, Hereafter better for mindful — you will not be wronged a thread.\n\nAlam tara ila alladhina qila lahum kuffu aydiyakum wa aqimu as-salata wa atu az-zakah — Those told restrain hands establish prayer give zakah — in Makkah period when not allowed fight.\n\nFalamma kutiba alayhim al-qitalu idha fariqun minhum yakhshawna an-nasa ka-khashyati Allah aw ashaddu khashyatan wa qalu Rabbana lima katabta alayna al-qitala lawla akhkhartana ila ajalin qarib — When fighting prescribed, group fear people as fear Allah or more and said why prescribed fighting, why not delay short term — lawla akhkhartana.\n\nQul mata'u ad-dunya qalil wal-akhiratu khayrun liman ittaqa wa la tuzlamuna fatila — Say enjoyment world little Hereafter better for mindful not wronged thread — fatil — tiny filament — same as not wronged fatila (49).\n\nFear people as fear Allah shows misplaced khashyah.\n\nAsking delay — lawla — shows love little enjoyment world.\n\nAnswer: mata' world little, akhirah better for mindful — same as better than beautified desires is Gardens (3:15).\n\nYou will not be wronged fatila — atom weight justice (39) — so fighting prescribed not wrong.\n\nNext wherever you are death will reach you even in lofty towers.",
  "74": "Wherever you are death will reach you even if you are in lofty towers — if good befalls them say this from Allah — if evil befalls say this from you — Say all is from Allah — what is wrong with people they hardly understand any statement? — Whatever good befalls you from Allah, whatever evil from yourself — We sent you as messenger to people — sufficient Allah as Witness.\n\nAyna ma takunu yudrikkumu al-mawtu wa law kuntum fi burujin mushayyadah — Wherever you are death reaches even lofty towers — buruj mushayyadah — fortified towers — death permission at written term (141) cannot avoid even if in houses those destined killed would go forth (150).\n\nWa in tusibhum hasanatun yaqulu hadhihi min indi Allah wa in tusibhum sayyi'atun yaqulu hadhihi min indik — If good befalls them say from Allah, evil say from you — blame messenger like hypocrites.\n\nQul kullun min indi Allah — Say all is from Allah — good and evil decree from Him — fa-ma li-ha'ula'i al-qawmi la yakaduna yafqahuna hadithan — What wrong people hardly understand statement?\n\nMa asabaka min hasanatin fa-min Allah wa ma asabaka min sayyi'atin fa-min nafsik — Whatever good befalls you from Allah, whatever evil from yourself — good from Allah bounty, evil from self due to what earned — earlier some earned causing Satan slip (161).\n\nWa arsalnaka lin-nasi rasulan wa kafa billahi Shahidan — Sent you messenger to people sufficient Allah Witness.\n\nTower imagery after wish delay: death reaches even towers, so delaying fighting not prevent death.\n\nAll from Allah in decree, but good from Allah bounty, evil from self earned.\n\nNext whoever obeys Messenger has obeyed Allah.",
  "75": "Whoever obeys Messenger has obeyed Allah — whoever turns away — We did not send you as keeper over them.\n\nMan yuti'i ar-Rasula fa-qad ata'a Allaha wa man tawalla fa-ma arsalnaka alayhim hafiza — Who obeys Messenger obeyed Allah — same as Messenger to be obeyed by permission Allah (63), obey Allah and Messenger so mercy (128), obey Allah Messenger best interpretation (58).\n\nMan tawalla — turns away — not sent as hafiz keeper over them — guardian — as earlier duty only convey (3:20, 2:119).\n\nObedience Messenger equals obedience Allah because Messenger conveys, purifies, teaches Book wisdom (3:164).\n\nAfter discussion death towers all from Allah, obedience Messenger is obedience Allah.\n\nNext they say obedience but when leave from you group spends night planning other than what you say.",
  "76": "They say obedience, but when they leave from you a group among them spends night planning other than what you said — Allah records what they plan at night — so turn away from them and trust Allah — sufficient Allah as Disposer.\n\nWa yaquluna ta'atun fa-idha barazu min indika bayyata ta'ifatun minhum ghayra alladhi taqul Wallahu yaktubu ma yubayyitun — They say obedience but when leave you group spends night planning — yubayyituna — other than what said.\n\nAllah records what they plan night — yaktubu — writes.\n\nFa-a'rid anhum wa tawakkal ala Allah wa kafa billahi Wakila — Turn away from them trust Allah sufficient Disposer — Wakil — as earlier sufficient Allah Wali Nasir, best Helper.\n\nNight planning — baytata — secret conspiracy night — as earlier those who cast pens, morning evening plot, those who distort words, those who say we hear disobey (45).\n\nTurn away — a'rid — same as turn away hypocrites (62) — private penetrating words etc.\n\nTrust Allah Wakil.\n\nNext do they not reflect on Quran? If from other than Allah would find much discrepancy.",
  "77": "Do they not reflect on Quran? Had it been from other than Allah they would have found much discrepancy.\n\nAfala yatadabbaruna al-Qur'an wa law kana min indi ghayri Allahi la-wajadu fihi ikhtilafan kathira — Do they not reflect — yatadabbaruna — tadabbur — deep reflection — on Quran? If from other than Allah would find much discrepancy — ikhtilaf kathir — many contradictions.\n\nInconsistency absent proves divine origin.\n\nEarlier (3:7) rasikhuna return mutashabih to muhkam believe all from Lord — tadabbur.\n\nThis verse after night planners: had they reflected Quran would see guidance not need night plotting.\n\nIt also answers those who claim Quran has contradictions — if from other than Allah would find many; since no, it's from Allah.\n\nTadabbur includes pondering stories, laws, promises.\n\nNext when news comes security fear they spread it — if returned to Messenger those in authority would know.",
  "78": "When news comes about security or fear they spread it — had they referred it to Messenger and those in authority among them, those who derive from it would know — were it not for Allah's bounty and mercy you would have followed Satan except few.\n\nWa idha ja'ahum amrun min al-amni aw al-khawfi adha'u bih — When comes matter security or fear they spread — adha'u — broadcast — hastily without verification.\n\nWa law radduhu ila ar-Rasuli wa ila uli al-amri minhum la-alimahu alladhina yastanbitunahu minhum — Had referred to Messenger and those in authority among them, those who derive — yastanbituna — extract, derive conclusion — would know.\n\nWa lawla fadlu Allahi alaykum wa rahmatuhu la-ittaba'tum ash-Shaytana illa qalila — Were it not bounty mercy you would have followed Satan except few.\n\nSpreading security/fear news without verification causes panic, false hope — similar earlier spreading news security fear they spread it (this) and spreading news morning evening plot etc.\n\nReferring to uli al-amr and Messenger ensures proper understanding.\n\nYastanbituna — from nabt — extraction — as extracting water, extracting ruling.\n\nFadl mercy includes Quran tadabbur, Messenger, authority.\n\nFollowing Satan except few — without guidance would follow.\n\nNext fight in Allah path you are responsible only for yourself and encourage believers.",
  "79": "Fight in Allah's path — you are responsible only for yourself — and encourage believers — perhaps Allah will restrain force of disbelievers — Allah stronger in force and more severe in deterrence.\n\nFa-qatil fi sabili Allahi la tukallafu illa nafsaka wa harrid al-mu'minina asa Allahu an yakuffa ba'sa alladhina kafaru Wallahu ashaddu ba'san wa ashaddu tankila — Fight path Allah you responsible only yourself — individual duty not conditional on others joining — like earlier faith individual witness.\n\nHarrid — encourage — believers.\n\nAsa Allah restrain force disbelievers — same as earlier cut off portion or suppress.\n\nAllah stronger force more severe deterrence — ashaddu ba'san ashaddu tankila — stronger force deterrence than disbelievers.\n\nAfter spreading security fear without verification, need encouragement not lagging.\n\nYou responsible only yourself — even if hypocrites lag (69) who lags behind, you still fight.\n\nNext whoever intercedes good intercession share, evil intercession share.",
  "80": "Whoever intercedes good intercession will have share of it, whoever intercedes evil intercession will have share of it — Allah over all Watchful.\n\nMan yashfa' shafa'atan hasanatan yakun lahu nasibun minha wa man yashfa' shafa'atan sayyi'atan yakun lahu kiflun minha wa kan Allahu ala kulli shay'in Muqita — Intercession — shafa'ah — good or evil — nasib — share — kifl — share burden.\n\nGood intercession: encouraging believers, reconciling, mediating justice, encouraging fight for weak.\n\nEvil intercession: discouraging, lagging, spreading fear, plotting night.\n\nNasib vs kifl — both share but kifl also burden.\n\nAllah over all Muqit — Watchful, Keeper — records intercession.\n\nLinks to earlier not take disbelievers as inner circle, do not take bitanah outside, encourage believers — shafa'ah good.\n\nNext when greeted with greeting greet better or return it.",
  "81": "When you are greeted with greeting, greet with better than it or return it — Allah over all Reckoner.\n\nWa idha huyyitum bi-tahiyyatin fa-hayyu bi-ahsana minha aw rudduha InnAllaha kana ala kulli shay'in Hasiba — When greeted with greeting — tahiyya — greet better or return it — hasan.\n\nTahiyya includes Salam alaikum, blessing.\n\nBetter than it — bi-ahsana — more complete: Wa alaikum salam wa rahmatullah.\n\nReturn it at least equal — rudduha.\n\nInnAllaha kana ala kulli shay'in Hasiba — Allah Reckoner — Hasib — counts greetings, knows.\n\nThis after intercession: even greeting intercession? Small social adab.\n\nHasib also earlier Allah suffices as Reckoner (6) for orphans.\n\nGreeting better encourages positive social fabric.\n\nNext Allah — there is no god except Him — will gather you Day no doubt — whose statement truer than Allah?",
  "82": "Allah — no god except Him — will surely gather you to Day Resurrection no doubt — whose statement truer than Allah?\n\nAllahu la ilaha illa Huwa la-yajma'annakum ila yawmi al-qiyamati la rayba fih wa man asdaqu min Allahi hadithan — Allah no god except Him will gather you to Day no doubt — same gathering earlier gather humanity Day no doubt (3:9), gathering inevitable (164).\n\nWa man asdaqu min Allahi hadithan — Whose statement truer than Allah? Hadith — speech — Allah most truthful, as earlier Allah has spoken truth follow millah Ibrahim (94).\n\nIf Allah truthful and will gather no doubt, then greetings, intercession, fighting for weak — all accounted.\n\nThis verse after greeting etiquette returns to grand tawhid and gathering.\n\nLinks to opening single soul creation — from single soul spread many — gathered back to One.\n\nNext why two groups concerning hypocrites while Allah cast them back for what they earned.",
  "83": "Why are there two groups among you concerning hypocrites while Allah cast them back for what they earned? Do you want to guide those whom Allah let stray? Whoever Allah lets stray you will find no way for him.\n\nFa-ma lakum fil-munafiqina fi'atayni Wallahu arkasahum bima kasabu — Why two groups concerning hypocrites while Allah cast them back — arkasahum — returned them to kufr for what earned.\n\nA-turiduna an tahdu man adalla Allah wa man yudlili Allahu fa-lan tajida lahu sabila — Want to guide those Allah let stray? Whoever Allah lets stray find no way.\n\nDisagreement after Uhud about hypocrites — some said kill, some said excuse.\n\nAllah cast them back — arkasahum — same as Satan made slip due to some earned (61) — earning caused return.\n\nGuidance after Allah let stray impossible if they insist.\n\nFor us, two groups concerning hypocrites still: treat lenient vs harsh; Quran says Allah cast back for what earned.\n\nNext they wish you disbelieve like they disbelieved so you become equal — do not take allies from them until emigrate path Allah.",
  "84": "They wish you would disbelieve as they disbelieved so you would be equal — do not take allies from them until they emigrate in Allah path — if they turn away seize and kill them wherever found — do not take from them ally nor helper.\n\nWaddu law takfuruna kama kafaru fa-takununa sawa'an fa-la tattakhidhu minhum awliya hatta yuhajiru fi sabili Allah — Wish you disbelieve like they so equal — same as wish turn you back after belief (3:69, 99).\n\nDo not take allies until emigrate — hijrah — emigration sign sincerity: leaving disbeliever camp to believers.\n\nFa-in tawallaw fa-khudhuhum waqtuluhum haythu wajadtumuhum wa la tattakhidhu minhum waliyyan wa la nasira — If turn away seize kill wherever found do not take ally helper — refers to combatants who turn away after emigration condition, not peaceful.\n\nContext of hypocrites actively plotting.\n\nNext except those join people with whom you have treaty.",
  "85": "Except those who join people with whom you have treaty or come to you with chests constricted from fighting you or fighting own people — had Allah willed He would have given them power over you and they would have fought you — if they withdraw not fight and offer peace — Allah has not made way for you against them.\n\nIlla alladhina yasiluna ila qawmin baynakum wa baynahum mithaqun aw ja'uka hasirat suduruhum an yuqatilukum aw yuqatilu qawmahum — Except those join people treaty or come chests constricted fighting you or own people — hasirat — constricted — hesitant.\n\nWa law sha'a Allahu la-sallatahum alaykum fa-laqatalukum — Had Allah willed given them power would have fought.\n\nFa-in i'tazalukum fa-lam yuqatilukum wa alqaw ilaykum as-salam fa-ma ja'ala Allahu lakum alayhim sabila — If withdraw not fight offer peace — salam — no way against them.\n\nThis verse after severe seize kill qualifier: exception for those with treaty or neutral whose chests constricted — they dislike fighting either side.\n\nIf withdraw offer peace, no way against them — no compulsion, no aggression against neutral peaceful.\n\nBalance: earlier fight for weak oppressed, fight allies Satan, but not against neutral who offer peace.\n\nShows Islamic war ethics not expansionist but defensive with peace offered respected.\n\nNext you will find others who wish secure from you secure from own people — whenever returned to fitna they fall into it.",
  "86": "You will find others who wish to be secure from you and secure from own people — whenever returned to fitna they fall into it — if they do not withdraw nor offer peace nor restrain hands seize kill wherever overtake — those We made clear authority over them.\n\nSa-tajiduna akharina yuriduna an ya'manukum wa ya'manu qawmahum kulla ma ruddu ila al-fitnati arkisu fiha — Others wish secure from you secure from own people — double-faced: want safety from Muslims and from disbelieving tribe — whenever returned to fitna they fall into it — arkisu — plunge.\n\nFa-in lam ya'tazilukum wa yulqu ilaykum as-salam wa yakuffu aydiyahum fa-khudhuhum waqtuluhum haythu thaqiftumuhum wa ula'ika ja'alna lakum alayhim sultanan mubina — If not withdraw nor offer peace nor restrain hands seize kill wherever overtake — clear authority — sultan mubin.\n\nThese are opportunistic double agents not neutral constricted but active fitting: want security both sides, but when fitna opportunity falls back into disbelief plotting.\n\nDifference earlier group constricted chests hesitant; this group whenever fitna returns plunge.\n\nIf they do not withdraw offer peace restrain hands, then clear authority to act.\n\nNext not for believer to kill believer except mistake.",
  "87": "It is not for believer to kill believer except by mistake — whoever kills believer by mistake then freeing believing slave and blood money handed to family unless they forgo as charity — if from people enemy to you while he believer then freeing slave — if from people treaty then blood money to family and freeing slave — whoever does not find then fasting two months consecutively — repentance from Allah — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nWa ma kana li-mu'minin an yaqtula mu'minan illa khata'an wa man qatala mu'minan khata'an fa-tahriru raqabatin mu'minatin wa diyatun musallamatun ila ahlihi illa an yassaddaqu — Not for believer kill believer except mistake.\n\nThen atonement: freeing believing slave, diya — blood money — to family unless forgo as charity — sadaqa — as earlier ujrat.\n\nIf victim from enemy people while believer — freeing slave only? Because family enemy not receive diya? But atonement still.\n\nIf from people treaty — mithaq — then diya to family and freeing.\n\nIf not find slave then fast two months consecutively — repentance — tawbah from Allah.\n\nWallahu Alimun Hakim — Knowing Wise — knows mistake vs intentional.\n\nThis verse after war ethics shows sanctity believer blood — not to be killed except mistake.\n\nFreeing slave as atonement links emancipation theme — encourage freeing.\n\nDiya — protects family rights.\n\nFasting two months consecutive shows seriousness.\n\nNext whoever kills believer intentionally recompense Hell.",
  "88": "Whoever kills believer intentionally — recompense Hell abiding therein — Allah angry with him, cursed him, prepared great punishment.\n\nWa man yaqtul mu'minan muta'ammidan fa-jaza'uhu Jahannamu khalidan fiha wa ghadiba Allahu alayhi wa la'anahu wa a'adda lahu adhaban azima — Intentional murder believer — recompense Hell abiding — khalid — same as curse abiding earlier — plus anger, curse, great punishment.\n\nGhadiba — angry — la'ana — cursed — a'adda — prepared great punishment — four punishments.\n\nIntentional killing believer enormous — after earlier do not kill yourselves Allah Merciful (29) and atom weight justice (39).\n\nDifference mistake atonement freeing fasting; intentional Hell anger curse great.\n\nShows why take precautions before fighting (68) and not take as inner circle those wish ruin (116) — to avoid killing believers mistakenly.\n\nNext O you who believe when go forth path Allah verify.",
  "89": "O you who believe, when you go forth in Allah's path verify — do not say to one who offers peace you are not believer seeking fleeting gain worldly life — with Allah are many gains — you were like that before and Allah favoured you — verify — Allah Aware of what you do.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu idha darabtum fi sabili Allahi fa-tabayyanu wa la taqulu li-man alqa ilaykum as-salam lasta mu'minan tabtaghuna arada al-hayat ad-dunya fa-inda Allahi maghanimu kathirah kadhalika kuntum min qablu fa-manna Allahu alaykum fa-tabayyanu — When go forth path Allah verify - tabayyanu — ensure.\n\nDo not say to one offers salam — peace, submission — lasta mu'minan — not believer — seeking fleeting gain — arada al-hayat ad-dunya — wanting spoils — as earlier beautified desires (3:14) worldly gain.\n\nFa-inda Allahi maghanimu kathirah — With Allah many gains — maghanim — spoils not limited.\n\nKadhalika kuntum min qablu fa-manna Allahu alaykum — You were like that before Allah favoured you — you also once hid Islam or were weak, Allah favoured guidance.\n\nFa-tabayyanu — Verify — repetition emphasizes.\n\nInnAllaha kana bima ta'maluna Khabira — Aware what you do — whether verify or hastily label disbeliever to take spoils.\n\nHistorical incident: group killed man who said Salam to take his sheep; verse revealed.\n\nLesson: verify before labeling, assume Islam from person offering peace, not accuse for worldly gain.\n\nAfter killing believer intentional Hell, now killing suspect without verification prohibited.\n\nNext not equal those who sit and those strive.",
  "90": "Not equal are those who sit among believers without excuse and those who strive in Allah's path with wealth and selves — Allah favoured strivers over sitters by degree — to both promised good — Allah favoured strivers over sitters great reward — degrees from Him forgiveness mercy — Allah Forgiving Merciful.\n\nLa yastawi al-qa'iduna min al-mu'minina ghayru uli ad-darar wal-mujahiduna fi sabili Allahi bi-amwalihim wa anfusihim faddala Allahu al-mujahidina ala al-qa'idina darajatan wa kullan wa'ada Allahu al-husna wa faddala Allahu al-mujahidina ala al-qa'idina ajran azima — Not equal sitters without excuse — qa'iduna — and mujahidun with wealth selves.\n\nFaddala Allah mujahidina ala qa'idina darajah — Favoured strivers over sitters by degree — plus great reward — darajat — degrees from Him forgiveness mercy.\n\nWa kullan wa'ada Allahu al-husna — To both promised good — husna — Paradise — because sitters may have excuse illness?\n\nAllah Forgiving Merciful — for perhaps sitters.\n\nThis verse after verification encourages striving not sitting with lagger who lags (69).\n\nDegrees from Him forgiveness mercy — darajat — varying degrees with Allah earlier (169).\n\nStriving with wealth selves — bi-amwalihim wa anfusihim — as earlier spend ease hardship, sell worldly for Hereafter.\n\nNot equal.\n\nNext angels take souls of those oppressed selves.",
  "91": "When angels take souls of those who wronged themselves — they say — Where were you? They say — We were weak oppressed in earth — Angels say — Was not Allah's earth spacious so you could emigrate? — Those refuge Hell — evil destination — except weak among men women children unable devise plan nor guided way — those perhaps Allah will pardon — Allah Ever Pardoning, Forgiving.\n\nInna alladhina tawaffahum al-malaikatu zalimi anfusihim qalu fi-ma kuntum qalu kunna mustad'afina fil-ard qalu a-lam takun ardu Allahi wasi'atan fa-tuhajiru fiha — Angels take souls of those wronged selves — asks where were you? They say weak oppressed earth. Angels: Was not earth spacious so emigrate? — Earth wasiatun — spacious — earlier Earth spacious so emigrate (150 commentary).\n\nFa-ula'ika ma'wahum Jahannam wa sa'at masira — Refuge Hell evil destination.\n\nIlla al-mustad'afina min ar-rijali wan-nisa wal-wildani la yastati'una hilatan wa la yahtaduna sabila — Except weak men women children unable plan nor guided way — mustad'afina truly weak not those who claimed weak while able.\n\nFa-ula'ika asa Allahu an ya'fu anhum wa kan Allahu Afuwwan Ghafura — Perhaps Allah will pardon — Afuwwan Ghafura — Pardoning Forgiving — Afuww — effaces sin.\n\nThis verse shows hijrah obligation when unable practice deen and earth spacious. Weak oppressed who could emigrate but did not — wronged selves.\n\nException truly weak unable devise plan nor guided.\n\nLinks to earlier take precautions go forth groups, fight for weak (71) — weak calling for guardian helper.\n\nNext whoever emigrates path Allah will find many refuges abundant.",
  "92": "Whoever emigrates in Allah's path will find many refuges and abundance — whoever leaves home emigrating to Allah and Messenger then death overtakes his reward has fallen upon Allah — Allah Forgiving Merciful.\n\nWa man yuhajir fi sabili Allahi yajid fil-ardi muraghaman kathiran wa sa'ah — Who emigrates path Allah finds many refuges and abundance — muragham — places go despite enemy, sa'ah — spaciousness — ample.\n\nWa man yakhruj min baytihi muhajiran ila Allahi wa Rasulihi thumma yudrikhu al-mawtu fa-qad waqa'a ajruhu ala Allah — Who leaves home emigrating to Allah Messenger then death overtakes reward fallen upon Allah — waqa'a ajruhu ala Allah — guarantee.\n\nWallahu Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving Merciful — for hardship emigration.\n\nThis encourages hijrah when weak oppressed — not fear lack refuge — many refuges abundance found.\n\nReward fallen upon Allah even if dies en route — intention counts.\n\nStory of man who emigrated from Makkah with illness? Actually old man? Reward upon Allah.\n\nAfter warning refuge Hell for those who could emigrate but didn't, now promise many refuges abundance for those who do.\n\nNext when you travel earth no blame shorten prayer if fear disbelievers may attack.",
  "93": "When you travel earth there is no blame if you shorten prayer if you fear disbelievers may attack — disbelievers ever open enemy to you.\n\nWa idha darabtum fil-ardi fa-laysa alaykum junahun an taqsuru min as-salati in khiftum an yaftinakum alladhina kafaru inna al-kafirina kanu lakum aduwwan mubina — When travel shorten prayer — qasr — if fear attack — fear.\n\nInna al-kafirina kanu lakum aduwwan mubina — Open enemy — aduww mubin — as earlier Satan open enemy (2:168, 4:27?).\n\nShortening prayer qasr concession for traveler — ease (27 lighten, 2:185 ease).\n\nIllness, journey, came from privy, touched women — allowed tayammum (43). Now travel shortening.\n\nPrayer guarded even fear (2:239) on foot riding, secure remember as taught.\n\nTravel shortening shows deen ease.\n\nNext when you among them and establish prayer for them.",
  "94": "When you are among them and establish prayer for them — let group stand with you taking arms — when prostrated let them be behind you and let other group not yet prayed come pray with you taking precautions arms — disbelievers wish you neglect arms and baggage so they attack with single assault — no blame if you lay down arms due to harm rain or ill but take precautions — Allah prepared for disbelievers humiliating punishment.\n\nWa idha kunta fihim fa-aqamta lahum as-salata fal-taqum ta'ifatun minhum ma'aka wal-ya'khudhu aslihatahum — When among them establish prayer for them — salat al-khawf — fear prayer — Prophet leads.\n\nLet group stand with you taking arms — asliha — weapons — when prostrated let be behind you second group not prayed come pray with you taking precautions arms — how salat al-khawf detailed.\n\nWadda alladhina kafaru law taghfuluna an aslihatikum wa amti'atikum fa-yamiluna alaykum maylatan wahidah — Disbelievers wish you neglect arms baggage attack single assault — so caution.\n\nWa la junaha alaykum in kana bikum adhan min matarin aw kuntum marda an tada'u aslihatakum wa khudhu hizrakum — No blame lay arms due rain harm ill but take precautions — hizr again.\n\nInnAllaha a'adda lil-kafirina adhaban muhina — Prepared humiliating punishment.\n\nPrayer fear shows even prayer not left in battlefield.\n\nArms precautions while praying shows balance tawakkul and hizr.\n\nHumiliating punishment for disbelievers who wish neglect.\n\nNext when completed prayer remember Allah standing sitting lying sides — when secure establish prayer — prayer on believers timed obligation.",
  "95": "When you completed prayer remember Allah standing sitting lying on sides — when secure establish prayer — prayer on believers timed obligation.\n\nFa-idha qadaytum as-salata fadhkuru Allaha qiyaman wa qu'udan wa ala junubikum fa-idha itma'nantum fa-aqimu as-salata inna as-salata kanat ala al-mu'minina kitaban mawqutan — When completed prayer fear remember Allah standing sitting lying — same as ulu al-albab remember standing sitting lying (3:191).\n\nWhen secure establish prayer — full form, not shortened fear.\n\nInna as-salata kanat ala al-mu'minina kitaban mawqutan — Prayer on believers timed obligation — mawqut — fixed time.\n\nRemembrance after prayer fear keeps connection.\n\nTimed obligation shows prayer not random but appointed times — as earlier guard prayers middle prayer (2:238) stand devout.\n\nFor travelers fearful, prayer time still fixed.\n\nNext do not weaken seeking people — if you suffer they suffer as you suffer while you hope from Allah what they do not hope.",
  "96": "Do not weaken in seeking people — if you suffer they suffer as you suffer — but you hope from Allah what they do not hope — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nWa la tahinu fibtigha'i al-qawm in takunu ta'lamuna fa-innahum ya'lamuna kama ta'lamuna wa tarjuna min Allahi ma la yarjun Wa kan Allahu Aliman Hakima — Do not weaken in seeking people — enemy — seeking — ibtigha.\n\nIn takunu ta'lamun — if suffer pain — ya'lamun — they suffer same as you suffer — both suffer.\n\nWa tarjuna min Allahi ma la yarjun — But you hope from Allah what they not hope — hope from Allah forgiveness, Paradise, victory — they hope worldly.\n\nThis encourages after prayer fear: do not weaken pursuing enemy.\n\nSuffering equal — earlier if wound touches you wound like touched others (3:136) — similar.\n\nHope difference — mu'min hopes what they not.\n\nAllah Knowing Wise — Knows suffering hope.\n\nNext We sent down Book in truth so you judge between people by what Allah showed.",
  "97": "We sent down to you Book in truth so you judge between people by what Allah showed you — do not be advocate for treacherous.\n\nInna anzalna ilayka al-Kitaba bil-haqqi li-tahkuma bayna an-nasi bima araka Allahu wa la takun lil-kha'inina khasima — Sent down Book truth so judge between people by what Allah showed — bima araka Allahu — not personal desire.\n\nWa la takun lil-kha'inina khasima — Do not be advocate for treacherous — kha'inina — treacherous, betrayers — like those who stole armor and accused Jew? Story of Tu'mah? Prophet almost defended Muslim thief? Revealed to judge justly even if against Muslim.\n\nBima araka Allahu — by what Allah showed — i.e., revelation, evidence.\n\nDo not be advocate for treacherous — even if Muslim, do not defend deceit to protect tribe.\n\nJustice principle — return trusts, judge justice (57), obey authority, return dispute to Allah Messenger (58), now judge by what Allah showed not advocate treacherous.\n\nNext seek forgiveness Allah — Allah Ever Forgiving, Merciful — next do not argue for those deceive themselves.",
  "98": "Seek forgiveness Allah — Allah Ever Forgiving, Merciful — and do not argue for those who deceive themselves — Allah does not love treacherous sinful.\n\nWastaghfiri Allaha InnAllaha kana Ghafuran Rahima — Seek forgiveness — istighfar — Allah Ever Forgiving Merciful — after judging error?\n\nWa la tujadil an alladhina yakhtanuna anfusahum InnAllaha la yuhibbu man kana khawwanan athima — Do not argue for those deceive themselves — yakhtanuna anfusahum — betray selves — Allah does not love treacherous sinful — khawwan athim.\n\nArguing for deceiver selves — earlier pleasing speech calls Allah witness what in heart most quarrelsome opponent (2:204) — argues.\n\nAllah does not love — la yuhibbu — as earlier not love arrogant boastful (36), not love transgressors, not love (39?) etc.\n\nTreacherous sinful — khawwan athim — opposite amin trustworthy.\n\nNext they hide from people but not hide from Allah while He with them when they plan.",
  "99": "They hide from people but cannot hide from Allah — He is with them when they spend night planning words He not pleased with — Allah encompassing what they do.\n\nYastakhfuna min an-nasi wa la yastakhfuna min Allahi wa Huwa ma'ahum idh yubayyituna ma la yarda min al-qawl wa kan Allahu bima ya'maluna Muhita — Hide from people but not hide Allah — He with them when they spend night planning words not pleased — yubayyituna — night planning same as group spends night planning other than what you say (76), Allah records what they plan night.\n\nAllah encompassing what they do — muhit — encompassing same as Allah encompassing (3:120) Allah encompassing what they do.\n\nHiding from people but not Allah shows nifaq.\n\nWith them — ma'ahum — with-ness knowledge not support.\n\nWords He not pleased — like accusing innocent Jew of theft, like ra'ina twist.\n\nAllah encompassing — muhit — cannot escape.\n\nNext here you are you argued for them worldly life but who will argue for them Day.",
  "100": "Here you are — you argued for them in worldly life — but who will argue for them on Day Resurrection? Who will be disposer over them?\n\nHa antum ha'ulai jadaltum anhum fil-hayat ad-dunya fa-man yujadilu Allaha anhum yawma al-qiyamati am man yakunu alayhim wakilan — Here you are argued for them worldly life — jadaltum — argued — but who will argue for them Day? — jujadil — and who will be wakil disposer?\n\nWorldly argument may succeed with eloquence — one more eloquent may win judge (hadith) — but Day no eloquence saves.\n\nWakil — disposer — as earlier sufficient Allah as Wakil (81).\n\nRhetorical: who will argue for treacherous self-deceivers Day? No one.\n\nSo do not argue for them now.\n\nNext whoever does evil or wrongs self then seeks forgiveness finds Allah Forgiving Merciful.\n",
  "101": "Whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks forgiveness will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful. Wa man ya'mal su'an aw yazlim nafsahu thumma yastaghfirillaha yajid Allaha Ghafuran Rahima — Who does evil — su' — against others — or wrongs self — sin personal — then seeks forgiveness — yastaghfir — finds Allah Ghafur Rahim.\n\nThis after admonition not argue for self-deceivers, hide from people not Allah — opens door: seeking forgiveness finds.\n\nGhfur Rahim again — Forgiving Merciful — as earlier seeking forgiveness Allah Ever Forgiving Merciful (98).\n\nSu' vs zulm nafs: evil against others vs self.\n\nFinds Allah Forgiving Merciful — yajid — finds — not merely may find but will find — guarantee.\n\nTawbah earlier defined as for those do evil ignorance repent soon (17).\n\nNext whoever earns sin earns only against self Allah Knowing Wise.",
  "102": "Whoever earns sin earns only against self — Allah Knowing, Wise. Wa man yaksib ithman fa-innama yaksibuhu ala nafsih wa kan Allahu Aliman Hakima — Earns sin only against self — as earlier (2:57) they did not wrong Us but wronged selves, and (3:117) Allah did not wrong them but wronged selves.\n\nAlim Hakim — Knowing Wise — knows sin, places recompense wisely.\n\nIthm — sin — earned — kasaba — acquisition.\n\nAfter forgiveness promise, reminds earning sin harms self.\n\nThis matches earlier no bearer burdens another — you earn against yourself.\n\nNext whoever earns fault or sin then accuses innocent has burdened slander great sin.",
  "103": "Whoever earns fault or sin then accuses innocent — has burdened slander and clear sin. Wa man yaksib khati'atan aw ithman thumma yarmi bihi bari'an fa-qad ihtamala buhtanan wa ithman mubina — Earns fault or sin then throws on innocent — yarmi — throws — bari' — innocent — has burdened buhtan — slander — and ithm mubin — clear sin.\n\nCase Tu'mah stole armor accused Jew? He earned sin theft then accused innocent Jew, burden slander.\n\nBuhtan — slander — as earlier take dowry qintar by buhtan clear sin (20).\n\nIthm mubin — clear sin.\n\nShows double sin: original fault plus false accusation.\n\nNext were it not for Allah bounty mercy upon you group would have misled you.",
  "104": "Were it not for Allah's bounty and mercy upon you, a group would have misled you — they mislead only themselves and cannot harm you at all — Allah sent down Book and wisdom and taught what you did not know — bounty great.\n\nWa lawla fadlu Allahi alayka wa rahmatuhu la-hammat ta'ifatun minhum an yudilluka wa ma yudilluna illa anfusahum wa ma yadurrunaka min shay'in wa anzala Allahu alayka al-Kitaba wal-hikmata wa allamaka ma lam takun ta'lam wa kana fadlu Allahi alayka azima — Had not for bounty mercy upon you group intended mislead you — la-hammat — intended.\n\nThey mislead only themselves — as earlier they mislead only themselves while perceive not (3:69).\n\nCannot harm you at all.\n\nAllah sent down Book wisdom taught what you did not know — as earlier teaching Book wisdom (2:129, 2:151, 3:164) what you did not know (2:151).\n\nFadl great — azim — bounty great.\n\nThis verse after self-accusation shows protection: Allah bounty mercy prevents misleading by night planners.\n\nBounty includes Quran, wisdom, knowledge what not know.\n\nGreat bounty — Owner great bounty (3:74).\n\nNext no good in much private conversation except who enjoins charity or good or reconciliation.",
  "105": "No good in much of private conversation — except who enjoins charity or good or reconciliation between people — whoever does seeking Allah pleasure We will give great reward.\n\nLa khayra fi kathirin min najwahum illa man amara bi-sadaqatin aw ma'rufin aw islahin bayna an-nas wa man yaf'al dhalika ibtigha'a mardati Allahi fa-sawfa nu'tihi ajran azima — No good in much private conversation — najwa — secret talk — except who enjoins charity — sadaqah — or good — ma'ruf — or reconciliation — islah — between people.\n\nWho does seeking Allah pleasure — ibtigha'a mardat Allah — same as those sell self seeking pleasure (2:207) and spend seeking pleasure (2:265) — We will give great reward — ajr azim.\n\nNajwa often negative — whispering, conspiracy, night planning other than what you say (76) — but exception three: charity, ma'ruf, islah.\n\nThis verse after group intended mislead — their secret conversation evil, but secret conversation enjoining charity good.\n\nGreat reward for seeking pleasure.\n\nLinks to earlier not take bitanah outside — secret talk with those wishing ruin no good — but secret talk enjoining charity good.\n\nModern private chats: what good in them? If enjoin charity, good, reconciliation — good.\n\nNext whoever opposes Messenger after guidance clear follows other than way believers.",
  "106": "Whoever opposes Messenger after guidance clear and follows other than way of believers — We will turn him to what he turned to and burn him in Hell — evil destination.\n\nWa man yushaqiq ar-Rasula min ba'di ma tabayyana lahu al-huda wa yattabi' ghayra sabili al-mu'minina nuwallihi ma tawalla wa nuslihi Jahannama wa sa'at masira — Who opposes Messenger — yushaqiq — splits from, opposes — after guidance clear — tabayyana — and follows other than way believers — sabil al-mu'minin — path believers.\n\nNuwallihi ma tawalla — Turn him to what he turned to — leave to own choice.\n\nNuslihi Jahannam — Burn Hell — sa'at masira — evil destination — same phrase earlier evil destination.\n\nWay of believers — sabil al-mu'minin — consensus? Following Ijma?\n\nOpposing Messenger after guidance clear is major — as earlier those claim believe but want taghut judgment, turn away aversion, etc.\n\nGuidance clear — as earlier Bayyinat.\n\nNext Allah does not forgive shirk forgives less than that.",
  "107": "Allah does not forgive that partners associated with Him but forgives less than that for whom He wills — whoever associates with Allah has strayed far.\n\nInna Allaha la yaghfiru an yushraka bihi wa yaghfiru ma duna dhalika liman yasha wa man yushrik billahi fa-qad dalla dalalan ba'idan — Same as 48 — Allah does not forgive shirk if dies upon, forgives less than that for whom wills.\n\nMan yushrik fa-qad dalla dalalan ba'idan — Strayed far — dalal ba'id — far astray — similar to Satan wants lead far astray (59).\n\nSecond occurrence same chapter to emphasize after opposition Messenger follows other than way believers — shirk worst opposition.\n\nShirk includes associating taghut as judge, taking allies besides Allah, consuming wealth of orphan etc? Root shirk?\n\nForgiveness less than shirk shows mercy vast.\n\nNext they call upon besides Allah none but females and call upon none but rebellious Satan.",
  "108": "They call upon besides Him none but females — they call upon none but rebellious Satan — Allah cursed him — Satan said I will surely take from Your servants portion appointed and mislead them, delude, order them cut ears cattle, order them change creation Allah — whoever takes Satan as ally instead of Allah lost clear loss.\n\nIn yad'una min dunihi illa inathan wa in yad'una illa Shaytanan marida la'anahu Allah wa qala la-attakhidhanna min ibadika nasiban mafruda — They call besides Him only females — inathan — idols named female — Lat, Uzza, Manat female names — and call but rebellious Satan marid — cursed.\n\nSatan said I will take portion appointed — nasib mafrud — share, mislead — udillannahum, delude — umanniyannahum, order cut ears cattle — fali-yubattikunna adhana al-an'am — pagan custom slitting ears cattle for idols, order change creation Allah — fali-yughayyirunna khalqa Allah — changing fitrah, tattooing, gender, etc.\n\nWa man yattakhidh ash-Shaytana waliyyan min duni Allahi fa-qad khasira khusranan mubina — Who takes Satan ally instead Allah lost clear loss — khusran mubin.\n\nSatan's plan matches earlier: threatens poverty orders immorality (2:268), wants deviate great deviation (26), tries make fear allies (3:175), weak plot (72).\n\nChanging creation includes changing fitrah, altering Book.\n\nNext Satan promises them deludes — not promise except delusion.",
  "109": "He promises them and deludes them — Satan does not promise except delusion. Ya'iduhum wa yumanni him wa ma ya'iduhum ash-Shaytanu illa ghurura — Promises and deludes — ya'id — promise — yumanni — wishful thinking, false hopes — as earlier gharrahum what they invented about religion by wishful lying (3:24), beautified desires made appealing (3:14), Satan threatens poverty orders immorality (2:268).\n\nWhat does he promise for those who consume orphan wealth, exchange bad good, take disbelievers allies seeking honour? He promises preservation wealth, increase via riba, protection via alliance, respect via arrogance boastful. All ghurur — delusion.\n\nWa ma ya'iduhum ash-Shaytanu illa ghurura — Satan promise only delusion — delusion evaporates like thin dust on smooth rock heavy rain leaves bare (2:264).\n\nPromises include wealth if keep orphan wealth?Actually loses Barakah. Promises honour if take disbelievers allies? Actually disgrace struck (3:110). Promises security if lag behind not fight? Actually regret in hearts (3:162). All delusion.\n\nNext those refuge Hell not find escape — destination of deluded.\n\nSo choice: favour from Allah being with blessed vs promises Satan delusion.\n\nNext refuge Hell no escape shows delusion ending.",
  "110": "Those — refuge Hell — they will find no escape from it. Ula'ika ma'wahum Jahannam wa la yajiduna anha mahisa — Those who followed Satan promises, worshipped females idols, took portion appointed by Satan, changed creation — refuge Hell — ma'wa — abode.\n\nWa la yajiduna anha mahisa — Will not find mahis — escape route, place to flee — no exit as earlier want exit Fire but not exit lasting punishment (5:54), no escape.\n\nContrast believers righteous refuge Gardens beneath rivers abiding forever (56) abundant shade.\n\nMahis — escape — none.\n\nAfter delusion promise, destination no escape.\n\nThis verse after Satan promises delusion closes his story.\n\nNext believers righteous Gardens promise Allah true whose statement truer.\n\nSo Hell no escape vs Gardens eternal.\n\nFor believer hearing, urgency to repent before no escape.",
  "111": "Those who believed and did righteous deeds — We will admit them Gardens beneath rivers flow abiding forever — promise Allah true — whose statement truer than Allah?\n\nWalladhina amanu wa amilu as-salihat sa-nudkhiluhum jannatin tajri min tahtiha al-anhar khalidina fiha abadan wa'da Allahi haqqan wa man asdaqu min Allahi qilan — Believed righteous admitted Gardens rivers eternal — promise Allah true — wa'da Allahi haqqan — as earlier truth from Lord (3:60, 60). Wa man asdaqu min Allahi qilan — Whose statement truer than Allah? — as earlier whose statement truer than Allah? (82) — same rhetorical: none truer.\n\nGardens vs Hell no escape contrast.\n\nWa'da true — Allah never breaks promise (3:9).\n\nWhose qilan — statement — truer? None.\n\nNext not by your wishful thinking nor People Book wishful thinking.",
  "112": "Not by your wishful thinking nor wishful thinking People Book — whoever does evil will be recompensed for it and will not find besides Allah guardian nor helper.\n\nLaysa bi-amaniyyikum wa la amaniyyi Ahli al-Kitab man ya'mal su'an yujza bihi wa la yajid lahu min duni Allahi waliyyan wa la nasira — Not by wishful thinking yours nor People Book — amaniyy — wishful — as earlier (2:111, 3:24) Fire few days etc wishful.\n\nMan ya'mal su'an yujza bihi — Who does evil recompensed for it — recompense exact — as earlier every soul paid full what earned (25, 82 etc) atom weight.\n\nWa la yajid... waliyyan wa la nasira — Will not find guardian helper besides Allah — same as sufficient Allah Wali Nasir.\n\nWishful thinking not save: \"We are beloved children Allah\"? No.\n\nAction matters.\n\nNext whoever does righteous deeds male female believing entered Paradise not wronged speck.",
  "113": "Whoever does righteous deeds — whether male or female — while believing — will enter Paradise and not be wronged even speck.\n\nWa man ya'mal min as-salihati min dhakarin aw untha wa huwa mu'min fa-ula'ika yadkhuluna al-jannata wa la yuzlamuna naqira — Righteous deeds male female while believing — mu'min — will enter Paradise not wronged speck — naqir — speck date seed — same as naqir earlier would not give speck (52) — now not wronged speck.\n\nNaqir small justice — as fatil filament (49), atom weight (39).\n\nMale female while believing — equality reward, as earlier Allah will not waste deed any doer male female you from one another (3:195).\n\nWhile believing condition — righteous deeds without iman not same.\n\nNext and who better in religion than one who submits face to Allah while doing good and follows religion Ibrahim upright — Allah took Ibrahim as close friend.",
  "114": "Who better in religion than one who submits face to Allah while doing good and follows religion of Ibrahim upright — Allah took Ibrahim as close friend.\n\nWa man ahsanu dinan mimman aslama wajhahu lillahi wa huwa muhsinun wattaba'a millata Ibrahim hanifan wattakhada Allahu Ibrahima khalila — Who better in religion than one who submits face to Allah while doing good — aslama wajhahu — as earlier (2:112) whoever submits face while doing good will have reward no fear grieve — and follows millat Ibrahim hanif.\n\nWattakhada Allahu Ibrahima khalila — Allah took Ibrahim as intimate friend — Khalil — highest love.\n\nAhsanu dinan — better religion — test: submit face, do good, follow Ibrahim hanif.\n\nFace submission — wajh — whole self as earlier.\n\nMuhsin — doing good.\n\nHanif — upright.\n\nKhalil — friend — status due submission.\n\nThis verse definition best deen after negating wishful thinking.\n\nNext to Allah belongs whatever heavens earth.",
  "115": "To Allah belongs whatever in heavens and whatever on earth — Allah ever encompassing all. Wa lillahi ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard wa kan Allahu bi-kulli shay'in Muhita — To Allah belongs heavens earth — repeated — Muhit — Encompassing.\n\nMuhita as earlier Allah encompassing what they do (4:98-99), encompassing disbelievers (2:19), encompassing plot (3:120).\n\nIf to Allah belongs all, Satan's promise delusion of ownership false.\n\nBelongs all — so wishful thinking not avail (112) not by wishful thinking yours nor People Book — recompense evil.\n\nEncompassing all means no escape from Hell (110) because encompassed, no hidden statement from Allah Day (41) will not hide.\n\nThis verse after not by wishful thinking and whoever does righteous male female believing enters Paradise not wronged speck — reminds all belongs Allah, recompenses justly speck naqir.\n\nEncompassing ensures justice atom weight.\n\nNext they ask you about women Say Allah gives ruling.\n\nAfter this, orphan woman questions.\n\nSo verse bridge from recompense to women rulings — both encompassed by Allah.",
  "116": "They ask you about women — Say Allah gives ruling about them and what recited in Book about orphan women you do not give what ordained while you desire marry them and about weak children and that you stand for orphans with justice — whatever good you do Allah Knowing.\n\nWa yastaftunaka fin-nisa quli Allahu yuftikum fihinna wa ma yutla alaykum fil-Kitabi fi yatama an-nisa allati la tu'tunahumma ma kutiba lahunna wa targhabuna an tankihuhunna wal-mustad'afina min al-wildani wa an taqumu lil-yatama bil-qist wa ma taf'alu min khayrin fa-inna Allaha kana bihi Alima — They ask about women — Say Allah gives ruling and what recited in Book about orphan women you do not give what ordained while desire marry them and weak children and that you stand for orphans with justice.\n\nEarlier verses orphan women (3) marry other women, now revisited.\n\nStand for orphans with justice — taqumu lil-yatama bil-qist — same as stand with justice earlier (57) when judge.\n\nWhatever good you do Allah Knowing — Alim knows.\n\nShows woman questions important; Allah answers.\n\nIncludes weak children — mustad'afin — earlier.\n\nNext if woman fears from husband nushuz or turning away then no blame reconciliation.",
  "117": "If woman fears from husband nushuz or turning away, no blame upon them if they reconcile between them — reconciliation better — souls are prone to stinginess — if you do good and are mindful Allah Ever Aware what you do.\n\nWa in imra'atun khafat min ba'liha nushuzan aw i'radan fa-la junaha alayhima an yusliha baynahuma sulhan wa-s-sulhu khayrun wa uhdirat al-anfusu ash-shuhh wa in tuhsinu wa tattaqu fa-inna Allaha kana bima ta'maluna Khabira — Woman fears nushuz — rebellion? Husband's? Actually nushuz husband turning away? If fears nushuz or i'rad turning away, no blame reconcile — sulh.\n\nSulh better — sulhu khayrun — reconciliation better — as earlier if fear breach send arbitrators desire reconciliation Allah will cause agreement (34) and reconciliation better, and no good in much private conversation except enjoin reconciliation (105).\n\nUhdirat al-anfusu ash-shuhh — Souls prone stinginess — shuhh — withholding, miserliness, clinging rights — makes reconciliation hard.\n\nWa in tuhsinu wa tattaqu — If do good and mindful — ihsan taqwa — Allah Aware what you do — Khabir.\n\nThis verse about marital discord where husband perhaps older not fulfilling rights, wife fears nushuz? Allows sulh e.g., wife waives some rights time, maintenance, to stay married, if both agree.\n\nSulh better than divorce.\n\nShuhh — stinginess — root many divorces.\n\nIhsan taqwa solution.\n\nNext you will never be able to be just between women even if strive — do not incline completely leaving like suspended.",
  "118": "You will never be able to be just between women even if strive — so do not incline completely leaving one like suspended — if you reconcile and be mindful Allah Forgiving, Merciful.\n\nWa lan tastati'u an ta'dilu bayna an-nisa wa law harastum fa-la tamilu kulla al-mayli fa-tadharuha kal-mu'allaqah — Never able just between women even if strive — justice in love feelings? Earlier justice required (3) if fear injustice one. Here explains absolute equity in love impossible — harastum — strive — but do not incline completely leaving like suspended — mu'allaqah — hanging, neither married fully nor divorced.\n\nWa in tuslihu wa tattaqu fa-inna Allaha kana Ghafuran Rahima — If reconcile and mindful Allah Forgiving Merciful.\n\nLan tastati'u an ta'dilu — never able — refers to heart love, not division nights maintenance which required just. So man must be just in what can control — time, support — not in heart inclination.\n\nMu'allaqah — suspended — cruelty: not divorcing nor fulfilling rights — similar to retain harm transgressing (2:231) and do not make Allah obstacle.\n\nIf reconcile mindful, Forgiving Merciful.\n\nNext if they separate Allah will enrich each from His abundance.",
  "119": "If they separate, Allah will enrich each from His abundance — Allah Vast, Wise.\n\nWa in yatafarraqa yughni Allahu kullan min sa'atih wa kan Allahu Wasi'an Hakima — If separate divorce, Allah will enrich each from abundance — sa'ah — spaciousness — not need cling to harmful marriage fearing poverty.\n\nAllah Wasi' Hakim — Vast Wise — Wasi' appears around provision, bounty, knowledge.\n\nAfter discussing sulh better, acknowledges separation may happen — if so Allah enriches each.\n\nEnrichment not only wealth but emotional, spiritual.\n\nWasi' — God bounty vast — provides without account (3:27, 3:37).\n\nNext to Allah belongs whatever heavens earth We enjoined those given Book before you and you to be mindful.",
  "120": "To Allah belongs whatever in heavens and whatever on earth — We enjoined those given Book before you and you to be mindful of Allah — if you disbelieve then to Allah belongs heavens earth — Allah Free of need, Praiseworthy.\n\nWa lillahi ma fis-samawati... wa laqad wassayna alladhina utu al-Kitaba min qablikum wa iyyakum an ittaqu Allaha — To Allah belongs heavens earth — We enjoined those given Book before and you be mindful — taqwa.\n\nWa in takfuru fa-inna lillahi ma fis-samawati... — If disbelieve then to Allah belongs heavens earth — He does not need your taqwa; benefit yours.\n\nWa kan Allahu Ghaniyyan Hamida — Free of need Praiseworthy — as earlier Self-Sufficient Praiseworthy (2:267) and Self-Sufficient (96,125).\n\nEnjoined taqwa to all given Book — same as first House? Actually covenant.\n\nTaqwa central.\n\nNext to Allah belongs heavens earth sufficient Allah as Disposer.",
  "121": "To Allah belongs whatever heavens earth — sufficient Allah as Disposer. Wa lillahi ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard wa kafa billahi Wakila — To Allah belongs heavens earth — sufficient Allah Wakil — Disposer — same as sufficient Allah as Guardian Helper (44), sufficient Allah Wali Nasir, sufficient Witness, etc.\n\nWakil — Disposer of affairs — as earlier trust Allah loves those trust (3:165), sufficient Disposer (4:81, 5:81).\n\nIf to Allah belongs all, why need worry if spouses separate Allah enrich each from abundance (119)? Because Disposer will dispose.\n\nWakil ensures inheritance fixed shares not random.\n\nAfter reminder Allah can take you away bring others Capable (122) — if disobey He replaces — because belongs all, disposes.\n\nSo sufficiency.\n\nNext if He wills He can take you away O people bring others.",
  "122": "If He wills He can take you away O people and bring others — Allah over that Capable. In yasha yudhhibkum ayyuha an-nasu wa ya'ti bi-akharina wa kan Allahu ala dhalika Qadira — If wills take you away — yudhhibkum — remove — bring others — as earlier if you turn back from religion Allah will bring people He loves they love Him humble believers stern disbelievers (5:91).\n\nWa kan Allahu ala dhalika Qadira — Capable over that — Qadir — as over all things Capable (3:26).\n\nAfter belonging heavens earth sufficient Disposer, warning He can replace.\n\nReminds dependency — you not essential; Ummah not permanent if turn away.\n\nAfter enjoining taqwa to those given Book before and you, if disbelieve to Allah belongs heavens earth Free need Praiseworthy — similar capability to replace.\n\nSo fear leaving weak offspring should prevent consuming orphan wealth etc because He can take you away.\n\nNext whoever desires reward world with Allah reward world Hereafter.",
  "123": "Whoever desires reward of world — with Allah reward of world and Hereafter — Allah Hearing, Seeing.\n\nMan kana yuridu thawaba ad-dunya fa-inda Allahi thawabu ad-dunya wal-akhirah wa kan Allahu Sami'an Basira — Who desires reward world — with Allah reward world and Hereafter — so ask Him for both, not only world.\n\nSami'an Basira — Hearing Seeing — hears desire, sees action.\n\nEarlier (3:145) whoever desires worldly gain We give it, whoever desires hereafter give, reward grateful — similar.\n\nWith Allah both rewards — so ask comprehensive — Rabbana atina fid-dunya hasanah wa fil-akhirati hasanah (2:201).\n\nNext O you who believe stand firm for justice witnesses for Allah even against yourselves.",
  "124": "O you who believe, stand firm for justice as witnesses for Allah even against yourselves or parents and relatives — whether rich or poor Allah more worthy both — do not follow desire so you deviate — if you distort or turn away Allah Ever Aware what you do.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu kunu qawwamin bil-qisti shuhada'a lillah wa law ala anfusikum awi al-walidayni wal-aqrabina in yakun ghaniyyan aw faqiran... — Stand firm justice — qawwamin bil-qist — as earlier return trusts justice (57) judge justice, stand for orphans justice (116).\n\nWitnesses for Allah even against yourselves parents relatives — strong.\n\nWhether rich poor Allah more worthy both — do not favour rich thinking better, nor poor pity distorting justice.\n\nFa-la tattabi'u al-hawa an ta'dilu — Do not follow desire so deviate — hawa — desire leads far astray (106).\n\nWa in talwu aw tu'ridu fa-inna Allaha kana bima ta'maluna Khabira — If distort or turn away Allah Aware what you do — talwu — twist tongue, turn.\n\nJustice requires standing even against self as earlier testimony tawhid.\n\nAfter reward world Hereafter, justice central.\n\nNext O you who believe believe.",
  "125": "O you who believe, believe in Allah and His Messenger and Book He sent down upon Messenger and Book He sent down before — whoever disbelieves in Allah, angels, Books, messengers, Last Day has strayed far.\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu aminu billahi wa rasulihi wal-kitabi alladhi nazzala ala rasulihi wal-kitabi alladhi anzala min qabl — O you who believe believe — aminu — believe — second belief deeper certainty — in Allah Messenger Book sent down upon Messenger and Book sent down before.\n\nWa man yakfur billahi wa malaikatihi wa kutubihi wa rusulihi wal-yawmi al-akhir fa-qad dalla dalalan ba'idan — Who disbelieves in Allah angels Books messengers Last Day strayed far — dalalan ba'idan — far astray as earlier Satan wants lead far astray (59) vs shirk far astray (107).\n\nBelieve in all Books not only Quran — as earlier no distinction between any (3:84, 2:136).\n\nIman in all components — creed.\n\nNext those believed then disbelieved then believed then disbelieved then increased disbelief not will Allah forgive nor guide path.",
  "126": "Those who believed then disbelieved then believed then disbelieved then increased in disbelief — Allah will not forgive nor guide them to path.\n\nInna alladhina amanu thumma kafaru thumma amanu thumma kafaru thumma izdadu kufran lam yakun Allahu li-yaghfira lahum wa la li-yahdiyahum sabila — Believed then disbelieved then believed then disbelieved then increased — pattern morning evening belief disbelief to cause return (3:72) and purchasing disbelief after belief (3:86-90 etc).\n\nLam yakun... li-yaghfira nor guide path — because increased disbelief until death? Persist.\n\nNot forgive nor guide — as earlier no guide wrongdoers, no forgiveness if dies disbelieving earth gold ransom.\n\nShows unstable faith of those use religion tactic.\n\nNext give tidings hypocrites painful punishment.",
  "127": "Give tidings to hypocrites that for them painful punishment — those take disbelievers as allies instead of believers — do they seek honour with them? Indeed honour belongs to Allah entirely.\n\nBashshiri al-munafiqina bi-anna lahum adhaban alima — Give tidings hypocrites painful punishment — bashshir — ironic tidings as earlier give tidings painful (21).\n\nAlladhina yattakhidhuna al-kafirina awliya min duni al-mu'minina ayabtaghuna indahum al-izzata fa-inna al-izzata lillahi jami'an — Take disbelievers allies instead believers — same as earlier not take disbelievers as allies instead believers (28), not take bitanah outside (116) — seek honour with them? Izzah belongs Allah entirely — as Owner honour (3:26) honours whom wills.\n\nSeeking izzah with disbelievers futile; izzah belongs Allah.\n\nHypocrites seek protection via alliance but honour belongs Allah.\n\nNext already revealed in Book if you hear signs disbelieved mocked do not sit with them.",
  "128": "Allah already revealed to you in Book that when you hear Allah's signs disbelieved and mocked do not sit with them until they enter other talk — otherwise you are like them — Allah will gather hypocrites and disbelievers in Hell all together.\n\nWa qad nazzala alaykum fil-Kitabi an idha sami'tum ayatillahi yukfaru biha wa yustahza'u biha fa-la taq'udu ma'ahum hatta yakhudu fi hadithin ghayrihi innakum idhan mithluhum — Already revealed in Book — in Al-An'am 68? — When hear signs disbelieved mocked do not sit with them until other talk — otherwise like them — complicity.\n\nInnAllaha jami'u al-munafiqina wal-kafirina fi Jahannama jami'an — Gather hypocrites disbelievers in Hell together — jami' — gatherer.\n\nSitting with mockers makes like them — as earlier listening attentively vs turning away.\n\nShows social adab: leave gathering where ayat mocked until other talk, else share.\n\nGathering Hell all together — as earlier desire equal (84) but equal in Hell not good.\n\nNext those waiting to see what befalls you — if victory from Allah they say were we not with you — if disbelievers have share they say did we not gain ascendancy.",
  "129": "Those who wait to see what befalls you — if victory from Allah you — they say were we not with you? — if disbelievers have share they say did we not gain ascendancy over you and protect you from believers? — So Allah will judge between you Day Resurrection — Allah will never grant disbelievers way over believers.\n\nAlladhina yatarabbasuna bikum fa-in kana lakum fathun min Allahi qalu a-lam nakun ma'akum wa in kana lil-kafirina nasibun qalu a-lam nastahwidh alaykum wa namna'kum min al-mu'minina — Those wait — yatarabbasuna — watching what befalls you — if victory from Allah you say were we not with you? Want share spoils; if disbelievers have share say did we not gain ascendancy over you protect you? Offer protection to disbelievers.\n\nFa-Allahu yahkumu baynakum yawma al-qiyamati wa lan yaj'ala Allahu lil-kafirina ala al-mu'minina sabila — Allah will judge between you Day, never grant disbelievers way over believers — sabila — way to wipe out believers completely.\n\nYatarabbasuna — waiting — same as those who wait (3:120?) Weak.\n\nTwo-faced: with believers when victory, with disbelievers when they have nasib.\n\nAllah will judge.\n\nNever grant disbelievers way over believers complete eradication — Islam remains.\n\nNext hypocrites try deceive Allah but He deceives them when stand for prayer stand lazily show people remember Allah little.",
  "130": "Hypocrites try deceive Allah but He deceives them — when they stand for prayer they stand lazily showing people and remember Allah but little.\n\nInna al-munafiqina yukhad'iuna Allaha wa Huwa khadi'uhum wa idha qamu ila as-salati qamu kusala yura'una an-nasa wa la yadhkuruna Allaha illa qalila — Try deceive Allah — yukhad'iuna — but He deceives them — khadi'uhum — recompense mirrors deed as earlier Allah mocks them (2:15) prolong transgression wandering blindly.\n\nWhen stand prayer stand kusala — lazily — show people — yura'una — riya as earlier spend to show people (37) and waste charity reminders (2:264).\n\nRemember Allah only little — qalila — little dhikr.\n\nDeceive Allah absurd — as earlier deceive none but selves not perceive (2:9).\n\nPrayer lazy shows hearts not firm.\n\nLittle remembrance opposite ulu al-albab remember standing sitting lying (3:191) and those standing praying in sanctuary (3:39) and remember much evening morning (41).\n\nNext wavering between — belong neither to these nor to these — whoever Allah lets stray you will find no way.",
  "131": "Wavering between — belonging neither to these nor to these — whoever Allah lets stray you will find no way for him.\n\nMudhabdhabina bayna dhalika la ila ha'ula'i wa la ila ha'ula'i wa man yudlili Allahu fa-lan tajida lahu sabila — Wavering — mudhabdhab — shaky between — not to believers nor disbelievers — neither.\n\nSame as two groups concerning hypocrites while Allah cast them back for what earned (83). Belong neither.\n\nMan yudlili Allahu — whoever Allah lets stray — as earlier wrongdoers not guided, devilish taghut guardians lead light darkness.\n\nNo way for him — no sabila — same as will not find way (83).\n\nWavering described for hypocrites: morning evening belief, if victory say were we not with you etc.\n\nModern wavering political: side where benefit.\n\nNext O you who believe do not take disbelievers as allies instead believers do you want make clear proof for Allah against you.",
  "132": "O you who believe, do not take disbelievers as allies instead of believers — do you want to make for Allah clear proof against yourselves?\n\nYa ayyuha alladhina amanu la tattakhidhu al-kafirina awliya min duni al-mu'minina a-tur... — Do not take disbelievers as allies instead believers — repeated third time (28, 44? Actually many times) emphasizing danger taking as inner allies seeking honour.\n\nA-tur... an taj'alu lillahi alaykum sultanan mubina — Do you want make for Allah clear proof against you — sultan mubin — clear authority — evidence — that you disobeyed.\n\nProof already revealed Book (128) not sit with mockers etc.\n\nTaking allies instead believers gives clear evidence against self Day.\n\nAfter wavering neither to these nor these, command not take disbelievers as allies instead believers — be clear side.\n\nNext hypocrites will be lowest depths Fire you will find no helper.",
  "133": "Hypocrites will be in lowest depths of Fire — you will find no helper for them.\n\nInna al-munafiqina fid-darki al-asfali min an-nar wa lan tajida lahum nasira — Lowest depths Fire — dark al-asfal — bottom, below disbelievers, because betrayal inside worse than outside enemy. Remember murder prophet, justice-orderers, etc? Hypocrisy more damaging.\n\nNo helper — nasira — same as no helpers earlier.\n\nDeepest Fire vs Gardens deep shade (56) abundant shade (zillan zalila).\n\nNext except those repent correct hold fast Allah purify religion for Allah — those with believers Allah will give great reward.",
  "134": "Except those who repent and correct and hold fast to Allah and purify religion for Allah — those with believers — Allah will give believers great reward.\n\nIlla alladhina tabu wa aslahu wa'tasamu billahi wa akhlasu dinahum lillah fa-ula'ika ma'a al-mu'minina wa sawfa yu'ti Allahu al-mu'minina ajran azima — Except repent — tabu — correct — aslahu — hold fast Allah — i'tasamu billah — as earlier hold fast rope Allah all together (3:103) — purify religion — akhlasu — for Allah — sincere, not for show.\n\nThose with believers — ma'a al-mu'minina — belong now, not wavering.\n\nAllah will give believers great reward — ajr azim — same as great reward responded after injury (3:177), great bounty Owner great bounty (3:74).\n\nFour conditions repentance hypocrites: repent, correct, hold fast Allah, purify deen for Allah.\n\nPurify deen — ikhlas — from riya, from taking disbelievers allies seeking honour.\n\nHolding fast rope Allah vs holding Taghut.\n\nWith believers — after wavering neither, now with.\n\nGreat reward.\n\nNext what would Allah do with punishment if you are grateful and believing.",
  "135": "What would Allah do with your punishment if you are grateful and believe? Allah Ever Appreciative, Knowing.\n\nMa yaf'alu Allahu bi-adhabikum in shakartum wa amantum wa kan Allahu Shakiran Alima — What would Allah do with punishment if grateful believing?\n\nAllah does not punish out of need; He is Ghani free need — as earlier if you disbelieve then to Allah belongs heavens earth free need Praiseworthy (120), Self-Sufficient does not need charity. Punishment not benefit Him.\n\nIf grateful believing — shakar — belief purification, He appreciates.\n\nShakiran Alima — Ever Appreciative, Knowing — Shakir — appreciates even small deed, Alim knows intention. Same as Allah Appreciative Knowing around charity? Earlier Allah Shakirun Halim (2:263) etc.\n\nIf you grateful believing, no reason punishment.\n\nThis verse soft after severe depths Fire — shows purpose not to torture but to guide; punishment only after persistence.\n\nGratitude belief protect.\n\nNext Allah does not love publicizing evil except who wronged.",
  "136": "Allah does not like publicizing evil speech except by one wronged — Allah Hearing, Knowing.\n\nLa yuhibbu Allahu al-jahra bis-su'i min al-qawli illa man zulim wa kan Allahu Sami'an Alima — Does not like publicizing evil speech — jahra bis-su — loud evil — except by one wronged — mazlum allowed raise voice about wrong.\n\nAllah Hearing, Knowing — Sami' Alim — hears publicized evil, knows wrong.\n\nPublicizing evil includes backbiting, slander, foul language — disliked.\n\nException mazlum — one wronged may speak about injustice to seek justice, as earlier kindness? But not exceed?\n\nHearing Knowing — hears jahra and knows if mazlum.\n\nNext if you disclose good or conceal it or pardon evil — Allah Ever Pardoning, Powerful.",
  "137": "If you disclose good or conceal it or pardon evil — Allah Ever Pardoning, Powerful.\n\nIn tubdu khayran aw tukhfuhu aw ta'fu an su'in fa-inna Allaha kana Afuwwan Qadira — If disclose good — tubdu khayran — open charity etc — or conceal — tukhfuhu — secret charity — or pardon evil — ta'fu an su' — as earlier pardon people (3:134) restrain anger — Allah Ever Pardoning Powerful — Afuwwan Qadira — Pardoning Powerful — able punish but pardons.\n\nAfter not love publicizing evil except wronged, says disclosing good or concealing good both okay — like earlier disclose charity good conceal better (2:271) — and pardoning evil — afw — same as pardon people.\n\nAfuwwan Qadira — combines pardon with power — pardons despite ability punish — model for believers: pardon while powerful, as earlier pardon them seek forgiveness consult.\n\nNext those disbelieve Allah and His messengers and want to differentiate between Allah and messengers.",
  "138": "Those who disbelieve in Allah and His messengers and want to differentiate between Allah and His messengers and say we believe in some and disbelieve in some and want to take way in between — they are truly disbelievers — prepared for disbelievers humiliating punishment.\n\nInna alladhina yakfuruna billahi wa rusulihi wa yuriduna an yufarriqu bayna Allahi wa rusulihi wa yaquluna nu'minu bi-ba'din wa nakfuru bi-ba'd wa yuriduna an yattakhidhu bayna dhalika sabila — Want differentiate between Allah and messengers — believe in some prophets disbelieve others — as Jews believe Musa not Isa Muhammad, Christians believe Musa Isa not Muhammad, some believe Allah but not messenger.\n\nWant take way between — sabila bayna — middle compromise.\n\nUla'ika hum al-kafiruna haqqa wa a'tadna lil-kafirina adhaban muhina — Truly disbelievers — haqqa — truly — prepared humiliating punishment — muhin — as earlier disgrace.\n\nThis after pardon power verses shows differentiating messengers not acceptable — same charter no distinction between any (3:84, 2:136).\n\nWay between — not Islam Way submission all.\n\nTruly disbelievers because reject part revelation after knowledge.\n\nNext those believed in Allah and messengers and did not differentiate.",
  "139": "Those who believed in Allah and His messengers and did not differentiate between any of them — We will give them their rewards — Allah Forgiving, Merciful.\n\nWalladhina amanu billahi wa rusulihi wa lam yufarriqu bayna ahadin minhum ula'ika sawfa nu'tihim ujurahum wa kan Allahu Ghafuran Rahima — Believed Allah messengers did not differentiate — same charter We make no distinction — will give rewards — ujur.\n\nAllah Ghafur Rahim — Forgiving Merciful — forgives past differentiation? Merciful reward.\n\nContrasts previous truly disbelievers humiliating punishment.\n\nBelieving all messengers is salvation.\n\nNext People Book ask you bring down upon them book from heaven — already asked Musa greater than that.",
  "140": "O People of Book ask you to bring down upon them a book from heaven — already they asked Musa greater — they said show us Allah plainly — thunderbolt seized them for wrongdoing — then they took calf after clear proofs — We pardoned that — We gave Musa clear authority.\n\nYas'aluka Ahlu al-Kitab an tunazzila alayhim kitaban min as-sama fa-qad sa'alu Musa akbara min dhalika fa-qalu arina Allaha jahratan fa-akhadhat-humu as-sa'iqatu bi-zulmihim thumma ittakhadhu al-ijla min ba'di ma ja'athum al-bayyinat fa-afawna an dhalika wa atayna Musa sultanan mubina — Ask bring down book heaven — as earlier those no knowledge say if only Allah would speak to us sign come same said before hearts alike (2:118) and People Book ask as Musa asked plainly (2:55 thunderbolt seized while looking).\n\nSa'iqa seized for wrongdoing — zulmihim.\n\nThen took calf after clear proofs — as earlier 2:51 when appointment Musa forty nights took calf while wrongdoers, 2:54 etc.\n\nAfaawna — pardoned — same as pardoned after calf (2:52).\n\nAtayna Musa sultanan mubina — Gave Musa clear authority — sultan mubin — clear proof — including Torah criterion.\n\nHistory repeats: demande show Allah plainly, worship calf, now demand book descend.\n\nNext We raised over them Mount and said enter gate prostrating and do not transgress Sabbath and took firm covenant.",
  "141": "We raised over them the Mount and said enter gate prostrating and say relieve us and do not transgress Sabbath — We took from them firm covenant.\n\nWa rafa'na fawqahum at-Tura bi-mithaqihim wa qulna lahum udkhulu al-baba sujjadan wa qulna lahum la ta'du fi as-Sabt wa akhadhna minhum mithaqan ghaliza — Raised Mount over them — Tur — as earlier took covenant raised mount over you take what We gave with strength remember what in it perhaps righteous (2:63) and mountain canopy they thought will fall (7:171).\n\nEnter gate bowing — sujjadan — as earlier enter gate bowing humbly say hittah — relieve burdens — forgive sins increase doers good (2:58).\n\nDo not transgress Sabbath — la ta'du fi as-Sabt — Sabbath transgression story.\n\nMithaq ghaliz — firm covenant — same phrase marriage firm covenant (20) — covenant with Prophets (81) — serious.\n\nMount raised reminder greatness covenant.\n\nThey broke covenant next verses.\n\nNext for breaking covenant disbelieving signs killing prophets.",
  "142": "So for breaking covenant, disbelieving Allah's signs, killing prophets unjustly and saying hearts are wrapped — rather Allah sealed them for disbelief — they believe not except few.\n\nFa-bima naqdihim mithaqahum wa kufrihim bi-ayatillah wa qatlihim al-anbiya bi-ghayri haqq wa qawlihim qulubuna ghulf bal taba'a Allahu alayha bi-kufrihim fa-la yu'minuna illa qalila — Breaking covenant, disbelieving signs, killing prophets unjustly — as earlier killing prophets (21, 181), and saying hearts wrapped — ghulf — covered — as earlier hearts sealed (2:7) hearing sealed eyes covering.\n\nBal taba'a Allahu alayha bi-kufrihim — Rather Allah sealed for disbelief — consequence — as earlier seal after refusal (2:7-10) disease increased.\n\nFa-la yu'minuna illa qalila — Believe not except few — qaleel.\n\nBreaking covenant, kufr signs, killing prophets, claim hearts wrapped — causes seal.\n\nFew believe — like Abdullah ibn Salam.\n\nNext disbelieving and saying about Maryam tremendous slander.",
  "143": "And for their disbelief and saying about Maryam tremendous slander.\n\nWa bi-kufrihim wa qawlihim ala Maryama buhtanan azima — Disbelief and saying about Maryam buhtan azim — tremendous slander — accusing her chastity, calling Isa illegitimate — huge slander.\n\nBuhtan azim — great slander — same as buhtan clear sin (20) and slander great sin (103).\n\nMaryam purified chosen over women worlds (3:42) chaste — slander severe.\n\nNext saying we killed Messiah Isa son Maryam messenger Allah — but they did not kill nor crucify but made to appear — those differ about it in doubt — no knowledge except following conjecture — did not kill certainly — but Allah raised him to Himself — Allah Mighty, Wise.",
  "144": "And saying we killed Messiah Isa son Maryam messenger Allah — but they did not kill him nor crucify but it was made to appear to them — those who differed about it are in doubt — no knowledge except following conjecture — they certainly did not kill him — but Allah raised him to Himself — Allah Mighty, Wise.\n\nWa qawlihim inna qatalna al-Masiha Isa ibna Maryama Rasula Allah wa ma qataluhu wa ma salabuhu wa lakin shubbiha lahum — Saying we killed Messiah — boast.\n\nWa ma qataluhu wa ma salabuhu wa lakin shubbiha lahum — Did not kill nor crucify but made appear.\n\nWa inna alladhina ikhtalafu fihi la-fi shakkin minh ma lahum bihi min ilmin illa ittiba'a az-zann wa ma qataluhu yaqinan — Those differed doubt — no knowledge except conjecture — did not kill certainly.\n\nBal rafa'ahu Allahu ilayh wa kan Allahu Azizan Hakima — Allah raised him to Himself — Mighty Wise.\n\nShubbiha lahum — made appear — Allah best planner (3:54).\n\nYaqinan — certainty — they did not kill.\n\nRafa'ahu — raised — same as will take you raise you to Me (3:55) purify you.\n\nAziz Hakim — Mighty Wise — Mighty to raise, Wise where place.\n\nThis verse core Isa not killed, cornerstone.\n\nNext there is none among People Book but will believe in him before death.",
  "145": "There is none among People Book but will believe in him before his death — Day Resurrection he will be witness against them.\n\nWa in min Ahli al-Kitabi illa la-yu'minanna bihi qabla mawtihi wa yawma al-qiyamati yakunu alayhim shahida — No People Book except will believe in him before his death — before Isa death after return? Or before person dying sees truth? Strong view: Isa will return before Hour and People Book believe in him as servant Messenger, not god.\n\nBefore his death — Isa's death after return.\n\nDay Resurrection he will be witness against them — Isa witness that he said Allah my Lord your Lord worship Him (5:117).\n\nShahid — witness as earlier nation witness, Messenger witness over these (40).\n\nThis verse after raising establishes return.\n\nNext for wrongdoing of Jews We forbade good foods made lawful.",
  "146": "So for wrongdoing of Jews We forbade good things that were lawful to them and for averting many from Allah's path and taking riba although forbidden and consuming people's wealth unjustly — prepared for disbelievers painful punishment.\n\nFa-bi-zulmin min alladhina hadu harramna alayhim tayyibatin uhillat lahum wa bi-saddihim an sabili Allahi kathiran wa akhdhihim ar-riba wa qad nuhu anhu wa aklihim amwala an-nasi bil-batil wa a'tadna lil-kafirina minhum adhaban alima — For wrongdoing Jews forbade tayyibat — good things lawful — earlier all food lawful except Israel forbade himself (3:93) but due to wrongdoing forbade more as punishment — fats etc.\n\nSaddihim an sabili Allah kathiran — Averting many from path — as earlier averting.\n\nTaking riba forbidden — as earlier do not consume riba multiplied (3:130).\n\nConsuming wealth unjustly — as earlier 2:188, 4:29.\n\nPrepared painful punishment — for disbelievers among them.\n\nTayyibat — good things forbidden as penalty — shows law can become stricter due to transgression — similar abrogation better similar concept.\n\nNext firm in knowledge among them and believers believe in what revealed to you and before.",
  "147": "But those firm in knowledge among them and believers believe in what was revealed to you and what revealed before you and establish prayer give zakah believe Allah Last Day — We will give them great reward.\n\nLakin ar-rasikhuna fil-ilmi minhum wal-mu'minuna yu'minuna bima unzila ilayka wa ma unzila min qablika wal-muqimina as-salata wal-mu'tuna az-zakah wal-mu'minuna billahi wal-yawmi al-akhir ula'ika sa-nu'tihim ajran azima — Firm in knowledge among them — rasikhuna fil-ilm — same phrase as (3:7) rasikhuna — those well-grounded say we believe all from Lord — now they believe what revealed to you and before.\n\nEstablish prayer — muqimina — give zakah — mu'tuna — believe Allah Last Day — will give great reward — ajr azim — same as great reward many times earlier.\n\nRasikhuna among People Book includes Abdullah ibn Salam etc believing Muhammad.\n\nGreat reward as earlier excellent reward workers, great bounty.\n\nNext We revealed to you as We revealed to Nuh and prophets after him.",
  "148": "We revealed to you as We revealed to Nuh and prophets after him — and to Ibrahim, Isma'il, Ishaq, Ya'qub and tribes, Isa, Ayyub, Yunus, Harun, Sulaiman — and to Dawud Zabur — and messengers We mentioned and not mentioned — and Allah spoke to Musa directly.\n\nInna awhayna ilayka kama awhayna ila Nuhin wan-nabiyyina min ba'dihi wa awhayna ila Ibrahima wa Isma'il wa Ishaq wa Ya'qub wal-asbati wa Isa wa Ayyub wa Yunus wa Harun wa Sulayman wa atayna Dawuda Zabura — Revealed to you as revealed to Nuh and prophets after — chain.\n\nWa rusulan qad qasasnahum alayka min qablu wa rusulan lam naqsushum alayka — Messengers mentioned and not mentioned — story not exhaustive.\n\nWa kallama Allahu Musa taklima — Allah spoke Musa directly — taklima — emphasis.\n\nRevelation pattern consistent: no new god.\n\nNuh first messenger after Adam, chain ends Muhammad.\n\nSupports (81) covenant prophets believe final messenger.\n\nNext messengers as bearers good news warners so people no argument after.",
  "149": "Messengers as bearers of good news and warners so people have no argument against Allah after messengers — Allah Mighty, Wise.\n\nRusulan mubashshirina wa mundhirina li-alla yakuna lin-nasi ala Allahi hujjatun ba'da ar-rusul wa kan Allahu Azizan Hakima — Messengers bearers good news warners so people have no argument after — hujjah — argument against Allah after messengers — i.e., cannot say no warner came.\n\nAllah Mighty Wise — Aziz Hakim — Mighty nothing overcomes, Wise sends messengers appropriate.\n\nMubashshir mundhir as earlier Muhammad deliverer good news warner (2:119,3:184?)\n\nPurpose remove excuse.\n\nNext but Allah bears witness to what He sent down to you He sent with His knowledge angels bear witness sufficient Allah as Witness.",
  "150": "But Allah bears witness to what He sent down to you — He sent with His knowledge — angels bear witness — sufficient Allah as Witness.\n\nLakin Allahu yashhadu bima anzala ilayka anzalahu bi-ilmihi wal-malaikatu yashhadun wa kafa billahi Shahida — Allah bears witness what He sent down to you — sent with His knowledge — ilmihi — as earlier He teaches what you did not know (104), knows what in heavens earth (29).\n\nAngels bear witness — as earlier Allah witnesses no god except Him and angels and people knowledge (3:18).\n\nKafa billahi Shahida — Sufficient Allah as Witness — as earlier sufficient Allah as Witness (41).\n\nIf Jews demand book from heaven (140), Allah witness suffices.\n\nKnowledge includes shaping wombs, provision without account.\n\nNext those disbelieved and averted from Allah path strayed far.",
  "151": "You will find others who wish secure from you and secure from own people — whenever returned to fitna they plunge — if they do not withdraw nor offer peace nor restrain hands seize kill wherever overtake — those We gave clear authority.\n\nSa-tajiduna akharina yuriduna an ya'manu kum wa ya'manu qawmahum kulla ma ruddu ila al-fitnati arkisu fiha fa-in lam ya'tazilukum wa yulqu ilaykum as-salam wa yakuffu aydiyahum fa-khudhuhum waqtuluhum haythu thaqiftumuhum wa ula'ika ja'alna lakum alayhim sultanan mubina — Find others wish secure from you secure from own people — want safety both sides double-faced, whenever returned to fitna plunge — arkisu.\n\nIf not withdraw nor offer peace nor restrain hands seize kill wherever overtake — clear authority — sultan mubin — evident permission.\n\nThose opportunistic not neutral constricted chests hesitant earlier (85) but active fitna plungers.\n\nDifference neutral constricted chests (85) hesitant dislike fighting either side, if withdraw offer peace no way against them; this group whenever fitna returns plunge — opportunistic.\n\nIf not withdraw offer peace restrain hands, clear authority.\n\nThis distinction important war ethics: neutral peaceful protected even if disbelievers; double agents who want security both sides but fall into fitna whenever chance and do not withdraw offer peace restrain, clear authority to act.\n\nFor today, similar: those who claim neutrality but whenever fitna opportunity plunge into harm.\n\nNext not for believer to kill believer except mistake — freeing slave, blood money, fasting.\n\nThis verse after distinguishing groups shows sanctity believer blood not to be killed except mistake, with atonement freeing slave, diya, fasting two months consecutive.",
  "152": "Those who disbelieved and wronged — Allah will never forgive nor guide to path except path of Hell abiding forever — easy for Allah.\n\nInna alladhina kafaru wa zalamu lam yakun Allahu li-yaghfira lahum wa la li-yahdiyahum tariqan illa tariqa Jahannama khalidina fiha abadan wa kana dhalika alalLahi yasira — Disbelieved wronged — combined kufr zulm — will never forgive nor guide except path Hell.\n\nLam yakun Allahu li-yaghfira — never forgive as earlier does not forgive shirk if dies upon.\n\nIlla tariqa Jahannama — Except path Hell — guidance to Hell as contrast guidance straight path.\n\nKhalidina abadan — abiding forever — as earlier curse abiding.\n\nWa kana dhalika alalLahi yasira — Easy for Allah — yasira — easy — as earlier burning Fire easy (30).\n\nAfter averting path far astray now never forgiven etc.\n\nNext O humanity Messenger has come with truth from Lord so believe better for you.",
  "153": "O humanity, Messenger has come with truth from Lord — so believe — better for you — if you disbelieve then to Allah belongs whatever heavens and earth — Allah Knowing, Wise.\n\nYa ayyuha an-nasu qad ja'akum ar-Rasulu bil-haqqi min Rabbikum fa-aminu khayran lakum wa in takfuru fa-inna lillahi ma fis-samawati wal-ard wa kan Allahu Aliman Hakima — O humanity — an-nas — universal — Messenger come with truth from Lord — bil-haqq — truth as earlier Book in truth (47, etc).\n\nBelieve better for you — khayran lakum — same as if People Book believed better for them (108).\n\nIf disbelieve then to Allah belongs heavens earth — as earlier to Allah belongs whatever heavens earth (115 etc) — free need.\n\nAllah Knowing Wise — Alim Hakim — knows who believes, places truth wisely.\n\nTruth from Lord — same as truth from Lord so not among doubters (60).\n\nEncourages belief universal after detailing People Book traits.\n\nNext O People Book do not exceed in religion say not about Allah except truth Messiah is messenger Word spirit from Him.",
  "154": "O People of Book, do not exceed in religion nor say about Allah except truth — Messiah Isa son Maryam is only messenger Allah and His Word He cast to Maryam and spirit from Him — so believe in Allah and His messengers and do not say three — desist better — Allah is only One God — Glory be to Him above having son — to Him belongs whatever heavens and whatever earth — sufficient Allah as Disposer.\n\nYa Ahla al-Kitab la taghlu fi dinikum wa la taqulu ala Allahi illa al-haqqa innama al-Masihu Isa ibnu Maryama Rasulullahi wa kalimatuhu alqaha ila Maryama wa ruhun minhu fa-aminu billahi wa rusulihi wa la taqulu thalathah intahu khayran lakum innama Allahu ilahun wahid Subhanahu an yakuna lahu walad lahu ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard wa kafa billahi Wakila — Do not exceed — ghulu — exceed limits — in religion — as Christians exceeded making Isa god.\n\nDo not say about Allah except truth — same as not say about Allah what not know.\n\nMessiah Isa son Maryam only messenger Allah and His Word He cast to Maryam and spirit from Him — Kalimah — Word Be, Ruh — spirit from Him created as Adam spirit? Not part of Him.\n\nDo not say three — Trinity — intahu khayran lakum — desist better for you.\n\nInnAllaha ilahun wahid Subhanahu an yakuna lahu walad — Allah One God Glory above having son — as earlier glory be Him (2:116).\n\nTo Him belongs heavens earth — sufficient Allah Disposer — Wakil.\n\nThis verse core tawhid vs Trinity.\n\nNext Messiah not disdain be servant Allah nor close angels — Whoever disdains disdainful and arrogant He will gather all to Himself.",
  "155": "Messiah would never disdain to be servant of Allah nor would close angels — whoever disdains to worship Him and is arrogant — He will gather them all to Himself.\n\nLan yastankifa al-Masihu an yakuna abdan lillah wa la al-malaikatu al-muqarrabun wa man yastankif an ibadatihi wa yastakbir fa-sa-yahshuruhum ilayhi jami'an — Messiah never disdains be servant — servant — abd — same as he said inni Abdullah (19:30) — nor close angels — muqarrabun — same as Isa among muqarrabin (45).\n\nIf he not disdain servanthood, how could he claim godhood? Servanthood honour.\n\nMan yastankif... yastakbir — Who disdains worship and arrogant — same disease Iblis refused arrogant became disbelievers (2:34) and those when told fear Allah arrogance takes in sin (2:206).\n\nSa-yahshuruhum ilayhi jami'an — Will gather all to Himself — hashr — gathering inevitable (164).\n\nSo angels close do not disdain servanthood; servanthood highest.\n\nNext as for those believed did righteous will pay wages in full and give more of bounty disdained arrogant will punish painful no guardian helper.",
  "156": "As for those who believed and did righteous — He will pay them wages fully and give more of His bounty — as for those who disdained and were arrogant He will punish painful — they will find no guardian nor helper besides Allah.\n\nFa-amma alladhina amanu wa amilu as-salihat fa-yuwaffihim ujurahum wa yaziduhum min fadlih wa amma alladhina istankafu wastakbaru fa-yu'adhdhibuhum adhaban aliman wa la yajiduna lahum min duni Allahi waliyyan wa la nasira — Pay wages fully — yuwaffihim — complete — and give more of bounty — fazl — as earlier best provision ridwan extra.\n\nThose disdained arrogant — istankafa wastakbara — punish painful — no guardian helper — same as no helpers earlier.\n\nWages fully vs painful punishment contrast.\n\nWali nasir same pair earlier sufficient Allah Wali Nasir.\n\nNext O humanity proof has come from Lord and We sent down to you clear light.",
  "157": "O humanity, proof has come to you from Lord and We sent down to you clear light.\n\nYa ayyuha an-nasu qad ja'akum burhanun min Rabbikum wa anzalna ilaykum nuran mubina — Proof — burhan — came from Lord — Muhammad, Quran? Burhan evidence.\n\nNur mubin — clear light — Quran — as earlier light vs darkness, Allah brings darkness light (2:257), Book light.\n\nBurhan and nur — proof and light — two descriptions: proof establishes, light illuminates path.\n\nAfter Isa not disdain servant, proof Messiah servant, now proof has come — Quran.\n\nClear light shows path straight.\n\nNext those who believe Allah hold fast to Him He will admit to mercy and bounty guide to straight path.",
  "158": "So those who believe in Allah and hold fast to Him — He will admit them into mercy from Him and bounty and guide them to straight path.\n\nFa-amma alladhina amanu billahi wa'tasamu bihi fa-sa-yudkhiluhum fi rahmatin minhu wa fadlin wa yahdihim ilayhi siratan mustaqima — Believe Allah hold fast Him — i'tasamu bihi — as earlier hold fast rope Allah together (3:103) and hold fast Allah purify (134) and hold fast Allah (134).\n\nAdmit mercy bounty — rahmat fadl — same as white faces in mercy (106) and bounty Owner great bounty.\n\nGuide to straight path — sirat mustaqim — same straight path worship Allah my Lord your Lord (51).\n\nMercy bounty guidance three rewards for belief holding fast.\n\nProof light now, holding fast leads admission.\n\nNext they ask you about kalalah say Allah gives ruling about kalalah.",
  "159": "They ask you about kalalah — Say Allah gives ruling about kalalah — if man dies no child and has sister — half what he left — she inherits him if no child — if two sisters two-thirds — if brothers and sisters male like share two females — Allah makes clear so you not go astray — Allah Knowing all.\n\nYastaftunaka quli Allahu yuftikum fil-kalalati ini mru'un halaka laysa lahu waladun wa lahu ukhtun fa-laha nisfu ma taraka wa huwa yarithuha in lam yakun laha walad — Kalalah — one dies no parent child but siblings — shares detailed.\n\nFa-in kanata ithnatayni fa-lahuma ath-thuluthani mimma taraka wa in kanu ikhwatan rijalan wa nisa fa-lidh-dhakari mithlu hazzi al-unthayayin yubayyinu Allahu lakum an tadillu Wallahu bi-kulli shay'in Alim — If two sisters two-thirds, if brothers sisters male like two females — similar inheritance earlier but kalalah specific.\n\nYubayyinu Allahu lakum an tadillu — Allah makes clear so you not go astray — bayan — as earlier Allah makes clear signs so you may be guided (102), makes clear verses so understand (2:242).\n\nWallahu bi-kulli shay'in Alim — Knowing all — same closing as many.\n\nKalalah verse final inheritance clarification, closes surah of women with emphasis clarity to avoid straying.\n\nThis final verse shows concern avoid going astray in division after detailed family laws — inheritance precise avoids dispute.\n\nFor today, kalalah still asked, clarity remains available written.\n\nEnds surah with bayan and All-Knowing.\n\nThus An-Nisa from single soul creation to inheritance kalalah all about ties, trusts, justice, mercy.",
  "160": "The surah now transitions from the theological discussion of Jesus to the practical consequences of the Jews' transgressions, specifically the dietary restrictions imposed as punishment. “We forbade the Jews certain foods that had been lawful to them for their wrongdoing.” This refers to the prohibitions mentioned in the Torah, such as the forbidding of certain fats, animals with claws, and other items that had previously been permitted. These were not part of the original, universal divine law; they were specific punitive measures for the Children of Israel because of their persistent rebellion and injustice. The verse explains the reason: “for their wrongdoing” (bi-ẓulmin minhum).\n\nThe word ẓulm encompasses their many sins: breaking the covenant, rejecting the prophets, indulging in usury, devouring people’s wealth unjustly, and all the crimes mentioned earlier in this passage. The dietary restrictions were a form of discipline, a yoke placed upon them as a consequence of their disobedience, making their religious practice more burdensome.\n\nThe verse then adds a second reason: “and for hindering many from the Way of Allah. ” They not only sinned themselves but actively prevented others from embracing the path of truth. They misrepresented the scriptures, hid the prophecies about the coming Prophet, and erected obstacles in the spiritual journey of the sincere seekers among both their own people and the Arabs. Their hindrance (ṣadd) was a major crime, multiplying their guilt. This verse provides a powerful lesson in the nature of divine law. Hardships and restrictions can sometimes be a consequence of collective sin. The mercy of Islam is evident in that the final law, the Shariah of Muhammad, is described elsewhere as a removal of burdens and shackles. It is a return to a purer, more merciful law.\n\nThe verse also warns believers that sin, especially when coupled with hindering others from guidance, can lead to the loss of divine blessings and the imposition of constraints, both spiritual and material. It sets the stage for the following verses that continue to detail the Jewish transgressions, particularly the taking of usury and consuming wealth unjustly.",
  "161": "The previous verse mentioned that certain foods were forbidden to the Jews as a consequence of their wrongdoing. This verse continues enumerating the specific transgressions that led to that punishment and their broader moral failures. First among them is “taking interest despite its prohibition.\n\n” The Arabic word is ribā, commonly translated as usury or interest, and it was explicitly forbidden in the Torah. Despite the clear divine command, many among the Jews engaged in ribā, exploiting the needy and profiting from the financial distress of others. This economic oppression was a direct violation of the covenant and a symptom of their hardened hearts, placing material gain above obedience to God.\n\nThe verse then adds a second, broader sin: “and consuming people’s wealth unjustly.” This covers every form of illicit financial gain: bribery, fraud, embezzlement, and the misappropriation of the property of orphans and the weak.\n\nThe phrase “unjustly” (bi al-bāṭil) means through falsehood and without any rightful claim. Together, these two crimes—interest and the unjust devouring of wealth—reveal a society where the powerful preyed upon the vulnerable, and where the love of wealth had supplanted the fear of God.\n\nThe verse then declares the consequence: “We have prepared for the disbelievers among them a painful punishment.” The specification “among them” is significant. It indicates that the punishment is not for all Jews indiscriminately, but for those who persisted in these grave sins and thus demonstrated disbelief in practice. The punishment is described as “painful” (alīman), emphasizing the severe suffering that awaits them in the Hereafter for their unrepentant economic exploitation. This verse offers a powerful lesson for all communities: economic injustice, particularly the taking of interest forbidden by Allah, is not a minor ethical lapse but a major sin that can lead to a painful divine punishment. It also serves as a warning to the Muslim community to uphold justice in all financial dealings, following the detailed inheritance and charity laws given earlier in this very surah.",
  "162": "After the severe condemnation of the sinful among the People of the Book, this verse opens the door of honour and reward for the righteous among them. It begins by describing the first group: “those of them well-grounded in knowledge.\n\n” The Arabic al-rāsikhūna fī al-ʿilm refers to scholars deeply rooted in authentic scriptural knowledge, whose learning leads them to humility and recognition of the truth rather than arrogance and denial. These are not the ignorant masses nor the corrupt leaders, but the sincere intellectuals and spiritual seekers among the Jews and Christians.\n\nThe verse then expands: “the faithful who believe in what has been revealed to you O Prophet and what was revealed before you.” This describes those who combine belief in the Qur’an with belief in the original Torah and Gospel. They do not see the final revelation as a contradiction but as a confirmation and completion, exactly as the earlier scriptures had foretold. Their faith is seamless.\n\nThe verse then highlights specific practices: “especially those who establish prayer—and those who pay alms-tax and believe in Allah and the Last Day.” These are the concrete manifestations of their comprehensive faith. They establish prayer (ṣalāh), the central act of worship connecting them to Allah; they pay the alms-tax (zakāh), fulfilling their duty to the poor; and their core belief is anchored in Allah and the Last Day, the foundation of all accountability. For such individuals, the promise is magnificent: “to these people We will grant a great reward. ” The reward is not a grudging acceptance but a truly great and abundant recompense. This verse powerfully illustrates that salvation is not about ethnic or religious labels but about sincere knowledge, comprehensive faith, and righteous deeds. It honors those among the People of the Book who, like ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām, recognized the truth of the Prophet and embraced Islam fully, while also acknowledging that their journey to faith was built on the authentic remnants of their own scriptures.",
  "163": "Having affirmed the believers among the People of the Book, the surah now establishes the unbroken chain of revelation that culminates in the Prophet Muhammad. The verse opens with the emphatic “Indeed, We have sent revelation to you O Prophet as We sent revelation to Noah and the prophets after him.” The revelation to Muhammad is not an anomaly or a break in divine communication; it is a continuation of the same sacred process that began with the first messenger after Adam, Noah. By mentioning Noah, the verse reaches back to the earliest roots of prophetic history, emphasizing the unity of the message.\n\nThe verse then proceeds to list a number of prominent prophets, grouping them in a significant order. “Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, and his descendants” covers the great patriarchs and the twelve tribes.\n\nThe mention of Ishmael alongside Isaac is a direct affirmation of the Arab branch of Abrahamic lineage, countering those who denied prophethood to the Arabs. Then comes “Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron, and Solomon,” a selection that includes prophets associated with patience (Job and Jonah), priesthood and support (Aaron), and magnificent kingship (Solomon), as well as Jesus, the central figure of the preceding discussion.\n\nFinally, the verse singles out David: “And to David We gave the Psalms.” The Psalms (Zabūr) are explicitly mentioned as a revealed scripture, a book of wisdom and praise. This entire list serves to remind both the Muslims and the People of the Book that the Prophet Muhammad is not a stranger to the prophetic tradition; he stands in a noble line of divinely guided men, receiving the same fundamental revelation: the call to the worship of the One God.\n\nFor the believer, this verse fosters a profound love and respect for all the prophets, and a deep sense of belonging to a community of faith that stretches across all of human history.",
  "164": "The verse continues the theme of the comprehensive nature of prophethood, now acknowledging that the list given in the previous verse is not exhaustive. “There are messengers whose stories We have told you already and others We have not.” The Qur’an contains detailed narratives of many prophets—Adam, Noah, Abraham, Lot, Moses, Jesus, and others—but there are many more whom Allah sent throughout history, to every nation, whose names and stories are not recounted in the Qur’an.\n\nThis is a profound statement. It teaches the believers that divine guidance is not limited to the Middle Eastern region or to the specific prophets they know by name. The mercy of Allah has reached all corners of humanity. It also protects the believer from the arrogance of thinking that their knowledge encompasses all of God’s dealings with humanity. There is a humility in recognizing that the divine plan is far vaster than what has been revealed to us in detail.\n\nThe verse then highlights the unique status of one particular messenger: “And to Moses Allah spoke directly.” The Arabic kallama Allāhu Mūsā taklīman uses a verbal emphasis that indicates direct, unmediated speech. While all prophets received revelation, Moses was given the distinct honor of hearing Allah’s speech without the intermediary of an angel.\n\nThis is why Moses is known as Kalīm Allāh, the one to whom Allah spoke. This verse, while acknowledging the countless unknown messengers, elevates the known ones by singling out Moses’ special distinction. It ties the entire discussion back to the earlier verses about the Torah and the covenant with the Israelites. The verse provides a balanced perspective: the Muslim community is part of a vast, global history of revelation, yet they are also recipients of a final, clear message, rooted in the same tradition that gave Moses the Torah and the direct speech of the Almighty.",
  "165": "This verse explains the unified purpose of all the messengers mentioned in the previous verses. “All were messengers delivering good news and warnings.” Every prophet was sent with a dual message: bashīr (bearer of glad tidings) and nadhīr (warner). The good news is for those who believe and do good, promising them Paradise and divine pleasure. The warning is for those who reject and disobey, alerting them to punishment and loss. This balance of hope and fear is the hallmark of all prophetic missions. It ensures that people are not driven solely by terror or lured solely by promise, but are moved by a combination that reflects the reality of a merciful but just Creator.\n\nThe verse then states the profound divine purpose behind this universal sending of messengers: “so humanity should have no excuse before Allah after the coming of the messengers. ” This is the principle of iqāmat al-ḥujjah, the establishment of proof. Allah, in His perfect justice, does not punish any people until He has sent them a messenger who clearly explains the truth and warns them of falsehood. After the messenger delivers the message, there is no longer any room for the plea of ignorance. Those who reject do so against clear evidence. This establishes the absolute fairness of the divine judgment on the Day of Resurrection. No soul will be able to say, “I did not know,” because Allah, in His mercy, sent guidance to every corner of the earth.\n\nThe verse concludes with “And Allah is Almighty, All-Wise.” The Almighty (ʿAzīz) sent messengers with a message that cannot be defeated, and He will hold humanity accountable with irresistible power. The All-Wise (Ḥakīm) designed this system of sending messengers as the perfect, wise method to guide free-willed beings, balancing mercy with justice. This verse fills the believer with gratitude for the gift of the Prophet and with a sense of responsibility, knowing that the excuse of ignorance has been removed.",
  "166": "After describing the purpose of the messengers, the verse directly addresses the Prophet with a comforting reassurance in the face of denial. “Yet if you are denied, O Prophet, Allah bears witness to what He has sent down to you.” The denial of the disbelievers does not diminish the truth of the revelation. The ultimate witness is not human acceptance or rejection, but the testimony of Allah Himself. When the Creator of the universe testifies to the truth of a message, any human denial becomes utterly insignificant.\n\nThis is a profound spiritual anchor for the Prophet and for every believer who faces rejection. The verse then explains the nature of this divine testimony: “He has sent it with His knowledge.” The revelation was not sent haphazardly or from a position of ignorance. It was sent down, saturated with Allah’s perfect, all-encompassing knowledge. Every word, every ruling, every historical account within the Qur’an is infused with divine wisdom and absolute accuracy. The knowledge of the One who knows the unseen, the past, and the future is the guarantee of the Qur’an’s truth. “The angels too bear witness. ” The noble angels, who are witnesses to the descent of revelation from the Preserved Tablet to the lowest heaven and then to the heart of the Prophet, also testify to its divine origin. Their pure testimony adds another layer of confirmation.\n\nThe verse then concludes with a powerful statement: “And Allah alone is sufficient as a Witness.” Even if all of humanity and the angels were to deny it, Allah’s testimony is enough. He is the ultimate, self-sufficient Witness whose acknowledgment validates everything. This verse is a fortress of faith for the believer. It teaches that our conviction in the truth of Islam should not be shaken by the disbelief of others, because the truth does not rest on majority opinion but on the unassailable witness of the All-Knowing Lord.",
  "167": "After affirming the divine witness to the truth of the revelation, the verse turns its focus back to the disbelievers, describing the depth of their misguidance. “Those who disbelieve and hinder others from the Way of Allah.” The verse identifies two distinct but often linked crimes.\n\nThe first is personal disbelief (kafarū): they reject the truth for themselves. The second, and even more destructive, is active hindrance (ṣaddū): they work to prevent others from reaching the path of Allah. They do not merely keep their disbelief private; they become obstacles, using mockery, arguments, persecution, and falsehood to block others from the truth. This dual crime amplifies their guilt tremendously, as they are not only responsible for their own misguidance but also share in the misguidance of every soul they lead astray.\n\nThe verse then pronounces the verdict on their state: “have certainly strayed far away. ” The Arabic ḍallū ḍalālan baʿīdan is a strong emphasis. Their straying is not a minor deviation but a deep, distant wandering from the straight path.\n\nThe word “far away” (baʿīd) indicates that the distance between them and the truth is immense, and the road back is long and difficult. This is the natural consequence of a heart that first rejects and then actively opposes. Each act of hindrance pushes them further into the wilderness of misguidance. This verse serves as a warning to the believers to never become a hindrance to others. It also provides a sobering analysis of why some rejectors are treated with particular severity in the Qur’an: because their sin extends beyond themselves.\n\nFor the Muslim, it reinforces the duty not only to be guided but to facilitate guidance for others, to be a means of opening the path, not blocking it. Conversely, it warns against those whose influence in society leads people away from the faith, marking their deviation as extreme.",
  "168": "The severity of the language intensifies. “Those who disbelieve and wrong themselves.” The disbelievers are also ẓālimūn, wrongdoers. Their primary wrong is the oppression of their own souls by denying the truth and suppressing their innate disposition toward faith. Every act of disbelief is an act of self-destruction, a wrong committed against the very self that is their most precious possession.\n\nThe verse then delivers one of the most terrifying verdicts in the Qur’an: “surely Allah will neither forgive them nor guide them to any path.” This is the state of those who have gone so far in their rejection and self-wronging that the doors of mercy and guidance are closed to them. They have died in a state of willful, persistent disbelief, having been given the clear message and ample time to respond. For such people, there is no forgiveness, because they have rejected the very source of forgiveness. And there is no guidance to any path—not just the path to Paradise, but no path of escape, no alternative route to safety. They are completely stranded in their spiritual ruin. The verse echoes the earlier statement in this surah about the hypocrites who oscillated in faith, but it applies universally to all who persist in disbelief and die upon it. It serves as the ultimate warning, a sobering counterbalance to the verses of mercy that precede and follow it. It is meant to shake the reader to the core, urging an immediate and sincere return to faith, because the state described here is final and irreversible.\n\nFor the believer, this verse fosters a profound gratitude for the gift of faith and a deep fear of ever straying, recognizing that the consequences of disbelief are not just a temporary setback but an eternal, total loss from which there is no recovery.",
  "169": "The previous verse stated that the disbelieving wrongdoers will not be guided to any path. This verse completes the statement by revealing the only path that remains for them. “Except that of Hell.” The particle “except” (illā) indicates that the negation of any path is not absolute in the sense of annihilation; there is one path left, and it is the most terrible one. They are not guided to the path of repentance, not to the path of Paradise, not to any path of escape or relief. The only road they will travel is the road that descends into the Fire.\n\nThe verse then emphasizes the eternal nature of their stay: “to stay there for ever and ever.” The Arabic khālidīna fīhā abadan uses a double emphasis to remove any possibility of the punishment ending. This eternity is the most terrifying aspect of Hell; it is not a rehabilitative sentence but a permanent state.\n\nThe verse then adds a phrase that magnifies the power of the Judge: “And that is easy for Allah.” The eternal punishment, which to human comprehension seems an infinite, crushing undertaking, is effortless for the Almighty. His power is not strained by sustaining the Fire and its inhabitants for eternity.\n\nThis statement serves as a direct refutation of any notion that the punishment described is too extreme or impossible. It reminds the disbeliever that the One they have defied is capable of this and more, without any difficulty.\n\nFor the believer, this verse instils a deep awe of Allah’s power and a profound fear of His punishment. It also, paradoxically, contains a comforting element: the same Allah for whom this is easy is also the One whose mercy is vast and whose entrance into Paradise is easy for those who believe. The ease of divine action is a double-edged sword, motivating both fear and hope. The believer is called to take the path of ease that leads to mercy, not the path of ease that leads to eternal justice.",
  "170": "After the terrifying depiction of Hell, the surah turns to a universal, merciful call. “O humanity! The Messenger has certainly come to you with the truth from your Lord.\n\n” This is a direct address to all people, across all times, announcing the undeniable fact of the Prophet’s arrival with the clear, unadulterated truth. The message is not a human philosophy or a cultural invention; it is “from your Lord,” who is the Creator and Sustainer of all.\n\nThe phrase “the truth” (al-ḥaqq) means that the message is factually correct, morally upright, and divinely guaranteed. The verse then gives the rationale for belief: “so believe for your own good.” Allah does not need your faith; you need it. Belief is not a favour you do for God; it is the sole means of your own salvation, purification, and eternal happiness. This simple statement reframes the entire call to faith. It is not a burdensome demand but a generous offer for your own ultimate benefit.\n\nThe verse then addresses the opposite choice: “But if you disbelieve, then know that to Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth. ” Disbelief harms only the disbeliever. It does not diminish Allah’s dominion, power, or majesty in the slightest. The entire universe is His, and He is not in need of any creature’s worship.\n\nThe verse concludes with a pair of divine names that have recurred throughout the surah: “And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise. ” He knows who believes and who rejects, and the wisdom behind the entire system of faith and accountability. This verse serves as a summary of the entire message: it is true, it is from your Lord, it is for your benefit, and your rejection of it is a loss only to yourself, while the Lord remains transcendent and unaffected. It is a final, open-handed invitation, stripped of all threat and grounded in pure logic and mercy.",
  "171": "This verse is a comprehensive theological address to the Christians, correcting the excesses that led to the doctrine of the Trinity and the divinity of Jesus. It opens with a direct call: “O People of the Book! Do not go to extremes regarding your faith.\n\n” The Arabic lā taghlū means to exceed the proper bounds, to exaggerate. The Christians are warned against the extreme of deifying their prophet and against the opposite extreme of the Jews in rejecting him. The command is clear: “say nothing about Allah except the truth.” All speech concerning God must be confined to what He has revealed and what is true, not what is fabricated by human speculation.\n\nThe verse then provides the correct, balanced truth about Jesus. “The Messiah, Jesus, son of Mary, was no more than a messenger of Allah.” This negates his divinity. He is a messenger, a human servant, not God. Then, “and the fulfilment of His Word through Mary. ” The “Word” is the divine command “Be,” through which Jesus was created in Mary’s womb without a father.\n\nThis is a miraculous act of creation, not an indication of divinity. “And a spirit created by a command from Him.” Jesus is a rūḥ, a spirit, meaning his creation was a direct, special act of Allah’s will. But he is a created spirit, not the uncreated God.\n\nThe verse then delivers the core command: “So believe in Allah and His messengers and do not say, ‘Trinity.’” The explicit prohibition of the term “Trinity” (thalāthah) is a direct refutation of the central Christian doctrine. The verse immediately follows with “Stop!—for your own good.” It is a merciful, urgent call to desist from a belief that leads to eternal ruin.\n\nThe verse then reaffirms the pure monotheism: “Allah is only One God. Glory be to Him! He is far above having a son!” The transcendence of Allah is proclaimed. He is too exalted to have offspring, which is a biological attribute of creation.\n\nFinally, the ownership of the universe and the divine sufficiency are reiterated: “To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And Allah is sufficient as a Trustee of Affairs.” The verse dismantles the theological basis of Christian doctrine with absolute clarity, replacing it with the pure monotheism of Islam, and it does so as a call to safety and truth.",
  "172": "Continuing the address to the Christians, the verse presents a powerful argument from the example of the most exalted beings. “The Messiah would never be too proud to be a servant of Allah.” The Christians who elevated Jesus to divinity did so with a misplaced sense of honoring him. But the verse declares that the true honor of Jesus lies precisely in his servitude to Allah, and that Jesus himself would never disdain that title. Being a servant of the Most High is the highest possible rank for any created being.\n\nThe verse then extends this to the highest ranks of creation: “nor would the angels nearest to Allah.” The angels brought near (al-muqarrabūn), the most honored and closest beings to the divine throne, do not consider themselves too great to serve and worship Allah. If Jesus and the archangels are not too proud to be servants, what justification does any human have for refusing to bow to their Creator?\n\nThe verse then transitions from the example of the humble to the fate of the arrogant: “Those who are too proud and arrogant to worship Him will be brought before Him all together.” The proud, both among humans and jinn, those who scoffed at the idea of submission, will be gathered on the Day of Judgment not as honored guests but as humiliated prisoners. Their arrogance will be stripped away, and they will stand before the One they refused to worship, facing His judgment.\n\nThe phrase “all together” (jamīʿan) implies a comprehensive, inescapable gathering. No one who displayed arrogance will be missed. This verse beautifully ties together the surah’s theology of servitude. The most noble of creatures—the Messiah, the angels—are proud to be slaves of Allah.\n\nThis is the ultimate honor. The true loser is the one who, out of false pride, refuses to join this company, and will instead be dragged before Allah as a defendant. The verse calls every human to embrace ʿubūdiyyah, servitude to God, as the path of the noble, following the example of the very best of creation.",
  "173": "This verse presents the final contrast between the two paths: humble servitude and arrogant refusal. “As for those who believe and do good, He will reward them in full and increase them out of His grace.” The believers who combine inner faith with outward righteous action are promised two things. First, the complete fulfillment of their due reward (yuwaffīhim ujūrahum). No good deed will be lost or diminished. The justice of Allah ensures that they receive exactly what they earned. Second, an increase (yazīduhum) from His grace.\n\nThis is the unbounded, unearned bounty of Allah, which multiplies rewards, grants higher stations, and bestows pleasures beyond imagination. This addition is a pure gift, reflecting the nature of a generous Lord who loves to exceed the expectations of His faithful servants.\n\nThe verse then turns to the opposite: “But those who are too proud and arrogant, He will subject them to a painful punishment.” Their sin is not just unbelief but istinkāf, a disdainful refusal and arrogance. They considered themselves above bowing to the Creator. Their punishment will match their crime: they will be subjected to a “painful punishment” that will break their false pride and leave them in utter humiliation.\n\nThe verse concludes with a repetition of the dire consequence: “And besides Allah they will find no protector or helper.” Their arrogance in this world led them to rely on themselves, their wealth, their patrons, or their false gods. But on that Day, all those supports will vanish. There will be no walī (protector) to shield them and no naṣīr (helper) to intercede or rescue them. They will be utterly alone, facing the wrath of the Almighty. This verse is a masterful summation of the surah’s central choice: humble, obedient faith leads to a reward that overflows with extra grace, while arrogant rejection leads to a punishment from which there is no escape.",
  "174": "The surah now delivers another universal address, similar to verse 170, summarizing the entire revelation as the ultimate proof and guidance. “O humanity! There has come to you conclusive evidence from your Lord.\n\n” The Arabic burhān means a clear, undeniable proof, an evidence that establishes the truth beyond any reasonable doubt. This “conclusive evidence” is the Qur’an itself, the final scripture, accompanied by the life and character of the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him. It is described as coming “from your Lord,” emphasizing that it is not a human invention but a direct communication from the Creator to His creation. This burhān leaves no room for the excuse of ignorance; the light has been lit, and whoever wishes to see can see.\n\nThe verse then uses a powerful metaphor: “And We have sent down to you a brilliant light. ” The Arabic nūran mubīnan means a light that is clear in itself and illuminating for everything else. The Qur’an is this light. In a world of darkness—darkness of ignorance, doubt, superstition, and moral confusion—the revelation is a brilliant light that makes the path clear. It allows the human being to distinguish truth from falsehood, good from evil, and the straight path from the crooked. The light not only illuminates the destination but also provides warmth, guidance, and hope. This verse is a declaration that the age of ambiguity is over. The evidence has been established, the light has been sent. Humanity is now divided between those who open their eyes to this light and walk in it, and those who turn away and remain in darkness. The verse serves as a final, gracious invitation, full of hope and clarity. It tells every human being: the truth you have been seeking, the proof you have been demanding, the light you need for your journey—it has arrived. What remains is your response.",
  "175": "The surah concludes the universal call with a beautiful promise that summarizes the entire spiritual journey. “As for those who believe in Allah and hold fast to Him.\n\n” The phrase “hold fast to Him” translates yaʿtaṣimū bi-Allāh. The root ʿaṣama means to grip firmly, to seek refuge and protection, to cling with all one’s strength. A believer is not merely someone who has a passive, intellectual assent; they are someone who actively clings to Allah, like a drowning person clinging to a rope.\n\nThis image of active, desperate dependence is the essence of true faith. The verse then describes the three stages of the divine reward. First, “He will admit them into His mercy. ” The believer is enveloped in the vast mercy of Allah, which is the source of all good and the shelter from all evil. Second, “and grace” (faḍl). Beyond mercy, there is an added bounty, a special favor that is not merely the removal of harm but the bestowal of overwhelming blessings and delights. Third, “and guide them to Himself through the Straight Path. ” This is the ultimate goal: arrival to Allah. The Straight Path (ṣirāṭ mustaqīm) is not just a road to Paradise; it is the road that leads to the divine presence itself. The verb “guide them” (yahdīhim) indicates that Allah will continue to guide them on this path until they reach their destination. This guidance includes the journey of this life, the moment of death, the stages of the Hereafter, and the final entry into the vision of Allah and His eternal nearness. This verse beautifully ties together the surah’s themes of faith, action, reliance, and divine reward. It presents the complete package of salvation: belief, clinging to Allah, and the threefold reward of mercy, grace, and guidance. It is a fitting conclusion to a surah that has detailed the laws and ethics that make up the Straight Path, ending with the promise that those who walk this path will be brought home, to the Lord who guided them all along.",
  "176": "The surah concludes by returning to its detailed theme of inheritance, specifically addressing the case of kalālah, a person who dies leaving neither parents nor children. The verse begins: “They ask you for a ruling, O Prophet.” The companions sought clarity on the inheritance of such a person, and the Prophet is told to respond, “Say, ‘Allah gives you a ruling regarding those who die without children or parents.’” The ruling is from Allah, not from the Prophet’s own opinion, ensuring its divine authority.\n\nThe verse then lays out the shares for siblings in this specific case. First, “If a man dies childless and leaves behind a sister, she will inherit one-half of his estate.” The full sister gets half. Second, “whereas her brother will inherit all of her estate if she dies childless.” If the sister dies in similar circumstances and leaves a full brother, he inherits everything. Third, “If this person leaves behind two sisters, they together will inherit two-thirds of the estate.” Two or more sisters share two-thirds. Fourth, “But if the deceased leaves male and female siblings, a male’s share will be equal to that of two females.” When the siblings are a mix of brothers and sisters, the distribution follows the familiar principle of the male receiving twice the share of the female, reflecting the greater financial responsibilities placed on men in Islamic law. This detailed ruling on kalālah fills the gap left by the earlier inheritance verses and provides a complete, just system. The verse closes with a powerful affirmation: “Allah makes this clear to you so you do not go astray. And Allah has perfect knowledge of all things.” The clarity of the divine law is a mercy meant to prevent error and dispute.\n\nThe verse ends where the surah’s inheritance discussion began—with the emphasis that these are limits set by the All-Knowing and All-Wise, whose perfect knowledge guarantees the justice of every share. The surah thus concludes its legislative masterpiece with a final note of clarity, divine authority, and the assurance that obedience to these rulings is the path of safety and righteousness."
};
